{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5","id":1511232,"title":"Hart Wardens Preview for W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T09:05:24-07:00","id":1511232,"title":"Hart Wardens Preview for W5","content":"<img width=\"1095\" height=\"700\" data-align=\"left\" data-linktype=\"2\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/RAchjcq.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/RAchjcq.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/RAchjcq.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Here's the preview for the Hart Wardens.<br /> <br /> The balancing (or lack thereof) of these Bans really reminds me of old-school Tribal/Clan-weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T10:03:26-07:00","id":1511234,"title":"","content":"Not impressed.<br /> No deep focus. Vague ''protector vibes'', and this ''one foot here and one here'' it's really not for my tastes.<br /> I expected a much more rustic vibe.<br /> Also, extremely strong forsaken vibes here, especially from the legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 05-10-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T10:45:12-07:00","id":1511239,"title":"","content":"Why is there a Tzimisce in Zulo form hanging out in the Werewolf picture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T11:22:14-07:00","id":1511242,"title":"","content":"Yet again, my biggest first impression, is that W5 cannot handle 11 playable Tribes and keep them meaningfully distinct. The electronic security specialist isn't a Glass Walker why? Because Glass Walkers can only &quot;build&quot; security systems, but you need to be a Hart Warden to care enough about protecting something to actually use it?<br /> <br /> The sudden dialect switch in the Emcee section was... unappealing. It sounds like someone who's closest connection to any hip-hop/rap communities is a third hand description of the 8 Mile movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T11:42:45-07:00","id":1511245,"title":"","content":"Talking about the &quot;Digital Caern Strategist.&quot; What exactly are they talking about here? Like what are they doing. I know they are comparing it to a strategy video game but, it comes off as a hollow reference. We can assume they are talking about the health of a caern including the security but, that's isn't really expressed here.<br /> <br /> Can I say that I also really don't care for the term 'Digital Caern.' It makes me believe they are making a caern in a digital space ... which I guess once could if you go by what the Digital web is in cWoD. I <i>know</i> they are talking about using electronics to manage a sept but, the way the information is presented is cringe as the kids say.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T11:55:36-07:00","id":1511246,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Favors of the two Tribe-previews I can already see that W5 is going down the same road as H5 with its Creed-fields in being really inconsistent... The Glass-Walker-Favor is: &quot;add one die to Technology or Science dice pools related to building or repairing things\u200b&quot; So whenever you build or repair something and the Technology- or Science-Skill is involved, you get an extra die. But the Hart Warden Favor is: &quot;add a die to any dice pool involving Survival, Animal Ken or nature-related Craft\u200b&quot; So... Hart Wardens get a die-bonus for two Skills... just in general <i>and </i>a die-bonus for &quot;nature-related&quot; Craft Skill-rolls. The Hart Warden Favor is clearly much better. Same deal with the Bans. The Hart Wardens one is much more situational than the Glass Walker one. It's far easier to avoid the Hart Warden Ban than the Glass Walker one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511242#post1511242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet again, my biggest first impression, is that W5 cannot handle 11 playable Tribes and keep them meaningfully distinct. The electronic security specialist isn't a Glass Walker why? Because Glass Walkers can only &quot;build&quot; security systems, but you need to be a Hart Warden to care enough about protecting something to actually use it?<br /> <br /> The sudden dialect switch in the Emcee section was... unappealing. It sounds like someone who's closest connection to any hip-hop/rap communities is a third hand description of the 8 Mile movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also comes up with the verbs (as many of us predicted). &quot;Cultivate&quot; and &quot;nurture&quot; is giving the same example of this verb in action twice.<br /> <br /> And the Emcee, yeah... Just immediately it starts with &quot;code-switchting&quot;... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:02:21-07:00","id":1511247,"title":"","content":"Well, the Huntsman is pissing me off. Because it is a job (even though the previous preview said jobs are HARD) but it is written as this groundskeeper of a manor. So it's just someone taking out excess deer from a British manor's lands. Very feral and very spooky. /s<br /> <br /> I might not be hunting myself, but I've had enough contact with the culture to say that they could have done this concept WAY better. Instead of a servant to a lord and lady, maybe they are an environmentalist hunting to protect the land until the wolves return. You know, actually upholding nature and not some manicured spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:06:42-07:00","id":1511248,"title":"","content":"The Huntsman thing annoyed me less, probably because I pretty much played that Fianna in a Victorian era set game. But you're right that the blurb in the preview doesn't really do anything to make it a modern-day relevant concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:11:33-07:00","id":1511249,"title":"","content":"I also find the idea expressed at the beginning way too broad. Taking nature and trying to preserve it in an &quot;untouched state&quot; so-to-speak and &quot;cultivating&quot; a bit of nature to become farmland are two <i>wildly different</i> outlooks on nature. I can't see two Hart Wardens with each of those outlooks working together. This Tribe should really have a unity-problem with such a broad idea of what it means to be a &quot;steward of nature&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:14:23-07:00","id":1511250,"title":"","content":"The main thing for me is that most of the actual description of the Tribe reads more like a general Garou primer rather than anything that should be speciifc to a particular Tribe ( once you remove the Stag Legend), all the stuff detailed is stuff ALL Garou should do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:15:33-07:00","id":1511251,"title":"","content":"What bothers me the most about the Huntsman is their image there. Like they have to make them look the most English possible just so you know that the Hart Wardens are totally English. I'm worried that Parawolf doesn't know that Irish and English are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:19:21-07:00","id":1511253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511248#post1511248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsman thing annoyed me less, probably because I pretty much played that Fianna in a Victorian era set game. But you're right that the blurb in the preview doesn't really do anything to make it a modern-day relevant concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a concept that matters outside a very specific way the game is set. As in your Victorian game. The Huntsman as a concept is made for settings where there are no native wolves to hunt the deer. Which isn't really the most common place WtA games are set in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:10:27-07:00","id":1511258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511251#post1511251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bothers me the most about the Huntsman is their image there. Like they have to make them look the most English possible just so you know that the Hart Wardens are totally English. I'm worried that Parawolf doesn't know that Irish and English are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably made her to look english not because she's a hart warden,specially since in W5 the Hart Wardens are Fromm all over the world and have no stronger ties to Ireland than anywhere else, they made her look as British as possible because her archetype is based on a archetype of a British hunstman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:13:01-07:00","id":1511259,"title":"","content":"Only now did I realize it was supposed to be the Fianna, now I wonder why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:18:30-07:00","id":1511261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511258#post1511258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably made her to look english not because she's a hart warden,specially since in W5 the Hart Wardens are Fromm all over the world and have no stronger ties to Ireland than anywhere else, they made her look as British as possible because her archetype is based on a archetype of a British hunstman</div> </div> </div> </div>No I get that but, given what has been said in recent and the fact they only changed the name of the Tribe from Fianna to Hart Warden recently. I'm inclined to give Paradox no rope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:19:55-07:00","id":1511262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511259#post1511259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only now did I realize it was supposed to be the Fianna, now I wonder why?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably because the Fianna were intimately tied with Celtic culture and the Hart Wardens are pan cultural . I have my reservations against a few of the separations of Garou tribes from human cultures but at the very least anyone can join any tribe.<br /> I totally get it that you guys are not feeling it though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:20:58-07:00","id":1511264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511261#post1511261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No I get that but, given what has been said in recent and the fact they only changed the name of the Tribe from Fianna to Hart Warden recently. I'm inclined to give Paradox no rope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:27:28-07:00","id":1511266,"title":"","content":"This feels very unpolished. None of these characters feel like Werewolves, for starters. None of the imagery evokes Rustic Nature Werewolf. And the idea that Stag introduced the Garou to nature... that opens a huge can of worms. It immediately makes no sense. Not for a single millisecond does it scan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:32:47-07:00","id":1511267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511262#post1511262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably because the Fianna were intimately tied with Celtic culture and the Hart Wardens are pan cultural . I have my reservations against a few of the separations of Garou tribes from human cultures but at the very least anyone can join any tribe.<br /> I totally get it that you guys are not feeling it though</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even know, kind of without that identity, but it seems that the Fianna, I'll continue to call them that, have become another completely different tribe. And what do you mean now anyone can enter? What was the restriction of the Fianna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:33:11-07:00","id":1511268,"title":"","content":"Ive been hearing a lot of &quot;x doesn't feel like a werewolf&quot; lately.<br /> what exactly makes someone a werewolf a opposed to something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:37:19-07:00","id":1511269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511267#post1511267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't even know, kind of without that identity, but it seems that the Fianna, I'll continue to call them that, have become another completely different tribe. And what do you mean now anyone can enter? What was the restriction of the Fianna?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding that it'd be at very least weird for a non celt to join the fianna,as well as a non native joint the uktena. It'd need some justification. But now all bqckground are welcome on all the tribes.<br /> I might have gotten something wrong though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-10-2023, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:47:47-07:00","id":1511270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511268#post1511268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive been hearing a lot of &quot;x doesn't feel like a werewolf&quot; lately.<br /> what exactly makes someone a werewolf a opposed to something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply to put; ferality and savageness. Each of these concepts should feel like they could become a ravening monster wolf in one second. To dip a bit into Forsaken imagery, the car liberator shouldn't CARE about human laws and focus on 'hunting' the fancy cars. Sell them to a chop shop and pocket the money gladly as it is theirs to take.<br /> <br /> To use a concept presented in Hart Wardens, the Huntsman should not be a servant to the gentry, but a hunter of another kind. Hunting deer to keep the overpopulation low but ALSO humans to keep the trophy hunters from overpopulating.<br /> <br /> The detective is not actually a detective, but someone you go to when you have no lawful way to bring someone to justice. The 'detective' will handle it and in the morning they find the wrongdoer torn to bits.<br /> <br /> These are not smooth vampires who try to cling to a thin veneer of civilization, these are savage monsters who tear their foes limb from limb and in some cases eat them. They are intense, feral and quick to anger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:51:08-07:00","id":1511271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511270#post1511270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply to put; ferality and savageness. Each of these concepts should feel like they could become a ravening monster wolf in one second. To dip a bit into Forsaken imagery, the car liberator shouldn't CARE about human laws and focus on 'hunting' the fancy cars. Sell them to a chop shop and pocket the money gladly as it is theirs to take.<br /> <br /> To use a concept presented in Hart Wardens, the Huntsman should not be a servant to the gentry, but a hunter of another kind. Hunting deer to keep the overpopulation low but ALSO humans to keep the trophy hunters from overpopulating.<br /> <br /> The detective is not actually a detective, but someone you go to when you have no lawful way to bring someone to justice. The 'detective' will handle it and in the morning they find the wrongdoer torn to bits.<br /> <br /> These are not smooth vampires who try to cling to a thin veneer of civilization, these are savage monsters who tear their foes limb from limb and in some cases eat them. They are intense, feral and quick to anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah now I get. I suspect (and this just a guess) that presenting a large variety of Archetypes was more important to the writing team than making all of the feel like a monster,again just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:58:06-07:00","id":1511272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511269#post1511269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my understanding that it'd be at very least weird for a non celt to join the fianna,as well as a non native joint the uktena. It'd need some justification. But now all bqckground are welcome on all the tribes.<br /> I might have gotten something wrong though</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really that hard to justify an unusual character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:58:46-07:00","id":1511273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511271#post1511271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah now I get. I suspect (and this just a guess) that presenting a large variety of Archetypes was more important to the writing team than making all of the feel like a monster,again just a guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the example characters don't feel like monsters, then the game shouldn't be about playing monsters. People will use those characters as reference points for how to play that specific creature/tribe/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:59:12-07:00","id":1511274,"title":"","content":"Oh sure, when the Fianna/Hart Wardens disembowel someone and string the entrails up on a tree, it's &quot;a strong message&quot;. But when the Red Talons do it, it's &quot;completely psycho&quot; and &quot;totally unjustified&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was my understanding that it'd be at very least weird for a non celt to join the fianna,as well as a non native joint the uktena. It'd need some justification. But now all bqckground are welcome on all the tribes.<br /> I might have gotten something wrong though\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being from a given human culture in Revised meant you were unlikely to have Pure Breed (that was lifted in W20, letting anyone have PB regardless of ethnic background). Basically, anyone could have a lineage associated with a tribe, as was even mentioned in the Revised Get of Fenris tribebook, and as of the most recent materials, they could also be a storied lineage of the tribe's heroes as reflected by PB. Some tribes were more willing than others to take different folks in; the Fianna wouldn't be as choosie as Older Brother, who has kinship chiefly with the dispossessed and oppressed indigenous peoples of the world, because the Fianna only care about being bard-ish and are more willing to sweep concerns like colonial privilege under the rug. The Red Talons, of course, won't let in any human cultures, and the Silver Fangs only come from the tribe's oldest and most established heroic lineages across Europe, Asia, and North Africa, but they're exceptional in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:59:48-07:00","id":1511275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511272#post1511272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it really that hard to justify an unusual character?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:01:16-07:00","id":1511276,"title":"","content":"Nods,nods. I see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:04:14-07:00","id":1511277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511270#post1511270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply to put; ferality and savageness. Each of these concepts should feel like they could become a ravening monster wolf in one second. To dip a bit into Forsaken imagery, the car liberator shouldn't CARE about human laws and focus on 'hunting' the fancy cars. Sell them to a chop shop and pocket the money gladly as it is theirs to take.<br /> <br /> To use a concept presented in Hart Wardens, the Huntsman should not be a servant to the gentry, but a hunter of another kind. Hunting deer to keep the overpopulation low but ALSO humans to keep the trophy hunters from overpopulating.<br /> <br /> The detective is not actually a detective, but someone you go to when you have no lawful way to bring someone to justice. The 'detective' will handle it and in the morning they find the wrongdoer torn to bits.<br /> <br /> These are not smooth vampires who try to cling to a thin veneer of civilization, these are savage monsters who tear their foes limb from limb and in some cases eat them. They are intense, feral and quick to anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>A reason this is doubly true for W5 is that on one hand the Garou aren't just these avatars of anger and rage but they're also supposed to be holy warriors with a mission (fight the Wyrm) and on the other hand, the context in W5 is supposed to be a mid-Apocalypse-setting where Gaia's dead/dying. Especially the latter part is really missing in these Tribe-writeups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:05:47-07:00","id":1511279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511269#post1511269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my understanding that it'd be at very least weird for a non celt to join the fianna,as well as a non native joint the uktena. It'd need some justification. But now all bqckground are welcome on all the tribes.<br /> I might have gotten something wrong though</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Most tribes will take anyone in as long as they are willing to work within the tribal strictures and are accepted by the totem. The only tribe that had an ethnic filter of who could join was Wendigo - who were strictly no people who aren't Native American (well and Red Talons, but that's something else). All the tribal cultures had certain preferences and their cultures took from certain human cultures, but there were no limitations to who could join based on their ethnicity.<br /> <br /> Also, what is a Celt in the 21st Century anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:54:13-07:00","id":1511285,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s too broad. Change for a new edition is fine if what we get is equal to, or better than, what we had before. It seems to me paradox was so worried of controversy that things are muddled down. The loud ones on the Twitter space may love it, but I feel for fianna fans here. <br /> <br /> could be well have more tribe development throughout the core though. This is really only 2 pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:03:18-07:00","id":1511286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511277#post1511277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A reason this is doubly true for W5 is that on one hand the Garou aren't just these avatars of anger and rage but they're also supposed to be holy warriors with a mission (fight the Wyrm) and on the other hand, the context in W5 is supposed to be a mid-Apocalypse-setting where Gaia's dead/dying. Especially the latter part is really missing in these Tribe-writeups.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much missing in any part of these preview. Nothing feels like there is any kind of urgency or want to do anything about what is/should be a real issue for the Garou of all tribes. What does it matter if you are have SoundCloud fans from Southwest Asia to the Baltics? Like is the complete death of your people and the world a joke to you where you do care anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thanked