oint of being lost to it. If everyone has completely given up the fight to the point of doing nothing then what even is the game anymore and why should we play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't say that is about survivor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:51:36-07:00","id":1511294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511279#post1511279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Most tribes will take anyone in as long as they are willing to work within the tribal strictures and are accepted by the totem. The only tribe that had an ethnic filter of who could join was Wendigo - who were strictly no people who aren't Native American (well and Red Talons, but that's something else). All the tribal cultures had certain preferences and their cultures took from certain human cultures, but there were no limitations to who could join based on their ethnicity.<br /> <br /> Also, what is a Celt in the 21st Century anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Fianna had the Firehair sub-tribe as well and SE Asia is a long way from Celtic. But yes, by Revised only Younger Brother had any real restrictions on what your human cultural background could be to be accepted by the Tribe...and even that could get over ridden by the Tribal Patron if they wished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:53:43-07:00","id":1511295,"title":"","content":"On a side note, holy shit the W5 official dice are fuck ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:57:09-07:00","id":1511301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511286#post1511286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very much missing in any part of these preview. Nothing feels like there is any kind of urgency or want to do anything about what is/should be a real issue for the Garou of all tribes. What does it matter if you are have SoundCloud fans from Southwest Asia to the Baltics? Like is the complete death of your people and the world a joke to you where you do care anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>So another theory I had,and it's a very unfounded one. Really it's just a bunch I have. It's that gaia's importance to the continuous existence,health and wellbeing of creation has been greatly overstated. It just might her possible death might not affect anyone or anything. It just might be she was unnecessary. The big conflict of the game just might &quot;ok we spent out entire existence dedicating ourselves to Gaia,what if we Dedicate ourselves... To ourselves?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:57:28-07:00","id":1511302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511267#post1511267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the restriction of the Fianna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that WtA treated Tribal weaknesses as optional (mostly because Pack Totems have them too). But since I didn't notice someone addressing this part:<br /> <br /> The old Fianna Weakness was +1 difficulty on Willpower rolls to represent the Tribe's penchant for passion and poor self-control.<br /> <br /> Stag's Ban as a pack Totem was that followers of Stag had to answer any request from aid from fae creatures or spirits, as well as always having to perform the Prayer for the Prey rite to the spirit of their kills after any hunt they participated in.<br /> <br /> So the concept of making their Tribal restriction a more generalized hospitality thing isn't a huge departure from previous material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:58:39-07:00","id":1511303,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing. But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them. Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:59:45-07:00","id":1511305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511301#post1511301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So another theory I had,and it's a very unfounded one. Really it's just a bunch I have. It's that gaia's importance to the continuous existence,health and wellbeing of creation has been greatly overstated. It just might her possible death might not affect anyone or anything. It just might be shenws unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... Did you ever read a Werewolf book? You know, from start to end? The whole point is that spirit and matter are intertwined. It's the literal foundation of the setting. As is the fact that Gaia dying is the Earth dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:00:26-07:00","id":1511306,"title":"","content":"the same problem of characters presented not being werewolves in the first place. The emcee and huntsman and the nerd could be used as writen to play a human+ rpg without any alteration. Those three are normal human beings doing normal human beings things. Even the images dont show any sign of werewolfnism.<br /> <br /> i feel that the nerd one is a copy of the urban planer one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 05-10-2023, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:00:47-07:00","id":1511307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511301#post1511301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So another theory I had,and it's a very unfounded one. Really it's just a bunch I have. It's that gaia's importance to the continuous existence,health and wellbeing of creation has been greatly overstated. It just might her possible death might not affect anyone or anything. It just might be she was unnecessary. The big conflict of the game just might &quot;ok we spent out entire existence dedicating ourselves to Gaia,what if we Dedicate ourselves... To ourselves?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> To add to this though,I must admit that it's more likely that the writers wants to reminds us that the Garou have lives. Interes hobbies,jobs families outside of their existence as werewolves. Their existence as Garou does not consume their entire life. To put it being a Garou might be part of who you are,not the entirety of who you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:02:34-07:00","id":1511308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511305#post1511305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... Did you ever read a Werewolf book? You know, from start to end? The whole point is that spirit and matter are intertwined. It's the literal foundation of the setting. As is the fact that Gaia dying is the Earth dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only read I few,and it's totally my fault I badly expressed that. So let it be know I'm a total werewolf noob.<br /> that being known,I'm theorising here, I don't expect the &quot;Gaia is not important theory&quot; to be true","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:05:22-07:00","id":1511309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511303#post1511303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing. But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them. Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how any of that works in setting, though. Spirits (and Falcon itself) are the arbiters of pure breed, not genetics tests or skin color. We know for a fact that there are groups of asian, african and arabic groups of Silver Fangs in addition to the ones descended from nobility of Europe.<br /> <br /> As for them denying good leaders, sure it's their problem, but at the end of day that's how you get Shadow Lords.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:13:06-07:00","id":1511310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511308#post1511308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I only read I few,and it's totally my fault I badly expressed that. So let it be know I'm a total werewolf noob.<br /> that being known,I'm theorising here, I don't expect the &quot;Gaia is not important theory&quot; to be true</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this may be a part of the reason why you get so confused when people react strongly to some of the things said by the dev team. You really have a lot of faith in them, and that's good for you. I hope the game works out for you. However, the ideas we're seeing and the sidestepping of core experience assumptions for Werewolf have made a lot of us wary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:15:16-07:00","id":1511311,"title":"","content":"No problem, I getcha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:16:10-07:00","id":1511312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511303#post1511303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing. But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them. Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did consider including the Fangs in that but as there are/were Silver Fang Houses throughout Europe, the America's, India, SEAsia, The Middle East, Siberia, Russia, Australia, they've got a fair bit of range even if it's just within a subsection of those communities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T17:23:42-07:00","id":1511313,"title":"","content":"I see Little Brother as highly likely to look the other way on the matter of adopting lupus cubs. Most tribes don't turn away wolf-born, so that might be one way that atypical members of Little Brother's tribe get in. After all, it's not their fault, and most wolves are in dramatic danger in the US and Canada, so they might feel a bit more of the tribe's plight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511307#post1511307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to this though,I must admit that it's more likely that the writers wants to reminds us that the Garou have lives. Interes hobbies,jobs families outside of their existence as werewolves. Their existence as Garou does not consume their entire life. To put it being a Garou might be part of who you are,not the entirety of who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet there's no discussion of even how their Rage or the shadow of their First Change affects them. The latter is particularly important, because you usually kill at least one person, and you have to live with those murders for the rest of your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T19:23:26-07:00","id":1511319,"title":"","content":"On the whole Gaia-thing, I think there used to be an idea there where defining what Gaia wants you to do was a more personal thing. I know it's a <i>wild</i> take on Gaia in WtA in general but it starts with the introduction in the preview in the Truths-section where it says: &quot;Werewolves are charged with an <b>unreliable </b>greater purpose by Gaia, a spiritual entity who is herself inherently <b>unknowable\u200b</b>&quot; (Emphasis mine). So you got that and if you look at the &quot;What Do Werewolves Do?&quot;-section, it pretty much mirrors what has been said in the Discord-Q&amp;A - with one exception:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I've noticed, V5 has its own specific style of play emphasizing the preservation of Humanity. Per my experience, H5 manifests as a mystery/survival style game. Is there a style of play that W5 will emphasize?<br /> From the introduction to the book, what do werewolves do?:<br /> \u2022 Fight to take back what has been lost<br /> \u2022 Building their own legend<br /> \u2022 <b>Define their relationship with Gaia</b><br /> \u2022 Explore the mysteries of the Umbra<br /> \u2022 Look out for others of their kind </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Of course that point &quot;defining your relationship with Gaia&quot; isn't there anymore. There are two more things: Back in July last year when Justin Achilli and Outstar talked about H5, they briefly mentioned W5 and JA talked about how werewolves would have Convictions similar to vampires and that their Convictions would be personal beliefs about Gaia. By October, though, similar to how the idea of &quot;Objects as Touchstones&quot; was jettisoned, the system of Convictions was also abandoned. But another thing that also links up with this wild take on Gaia is that JA mentioned back in October how Gaia-affiliated spirits can also be antagonists to Garou.<br /> <br /> I guess, we'll see with the whole write-up how much of this idea of &quot;defining your personal relationship with Gaia&quot; is still in there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T23:08:52-07:00","id":1511330,"title":"","content":"Trying to explain my point better.<br /> <br /> First off, I overall like w5 ideas for various reasons and also because I am a fan of werewolves in general. But I am intelligent enough to understand people's skepticism and mistrust. I am very cold about the various editions. Now I have 5 edition of werewolf and if w5 will end up in dust in my shelf no problem no hard feeling I have 4 other editions to chose. I like them all.<br /> <br /> Why I am saying this ? just to be sure you understand that I'm trying being pragmatical as much as I can.<br /> <br /> That being said, the problem about Hart Wardens from what I see is the totally lack of focus. I like the overall description as protectors but it clashes both whith some archetypes as much as other things.<br /> The fact they are a tribe that stays with one foot in society and one foot outside makes the tribe totally unfocused and vague in its nature.<br /> a tribe, by definition, is militant. Not in the sense of politics or social ideas but by the fact that &quot; I'm part of my tribe and we do x things because of y &quot;. Even CoG or Silent strider are militant in some ways.<br /> This part is absent especially when we read the archetypes. The huntsman and the urban legend are kinda ok because their vibe is much more rustic and in line with the totem but still, they can be part or every tribe but not as much as the other 2 archetypes which can be... almost everything, especially glass walkers or bone gnawers. That means that every kind of &quot;protector&quot; or &quot;bard&quot; could be part of the tribe, but this helps to destroy the focus, the &quot;why&quot; the Hart Wardens cooperate and are United.<br /> <br /> I really cant see how a emcee like pack and a hillbilly slasher like pack can get along just because the have Stag as totem. I really, as a storyteller, dont know how to fit in a pack two different characters like, the wolf farmer and the techno modern barbarian that use technology to spread stories. What the fuck I'm supposed to do with Stag here ?<br /> <br /> just my opinion.<br /> this preview really left me cold as a fianna fan from the older editions.<br /> ok the point is, you can play whichever character you want with whatever profile, just make him a protector or a welcoming but traditional bard or host, but still. Again, I understand they wanted to create conceptual tribe and &quot;create your local version of your tribe&quot;, but like forsaken 2 teach us, even if you create something conceptual, you can put focus on it. What are the galestalkers be? Cold people? Wtf. <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit : this kind of stuff is the kind of stuff that will make people play Get of Fenris and Stargazers home ruling the fuck out of them because , mark my word, their descriptions will be more focused and centred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 05-11-2023, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T23:33:18-07:00","id":1511331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511307#post1511307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to this though,I must admit that it's more likely that the writers wants to reminds us that the Garou have lives. Interes hobbies,jobs families outside of their existence as werewolves. Their existence as Garou does not consume their entire life. To put it being a Garou might be part of who you are,not the entirety of who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something the players do, though. The book should be showing how the werewolf side of the character behaves and the players add the human side.<br /> <br /> As you are a Werewolf noob, let me be honest; This has been an ongoing issue with WtA books. The core sets up these hard limits and then tribebooks/others ignore them because it limits the characters they'd write too much. W5 COULD have avoided this and just let garou have human relations, but then they had to add that one sidebar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T23:40:12-07:00","id":1511332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511293#post1511293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They didn't say that is about survivor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly? Heroic stuff is in the past, now Garou suppose to fight just to survive one more day. The big game is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T01:07:27-07:00","id":1511335,"title":"","content":"We're so hospitable, welcome, feel at home, I will fucking skin you if you feel too at home though... anyhow, yes.<br /> <br /> Gives me &quot;why don't these bitches give me sex; don't they understand I'm a nice guy?&quot; kind of vibes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of bitches and sex, I feel like there's a fundamental misunderstanding of Stag's symbolism here, at least insofar as it was used by the Fianna. Fianna were always the party tribe who were boisterous, drunk, promiscuous and fond of telling tall tales to impress others. They were overly passionate. It made sense they followed stag, because that's kinda how Stags work. The defining feature of stags are the antlers, and they get big impressive antlers to impress the ladies and intimidate others, they wrestle other stags, the winner gets mating rights. That's Fianna life in a nutshell. Oh sure they adhere to the idea of being honourably mated but if that worked in practice they wouldn't be making so many metis. Maybe the reason they hated metis so much is because they're not good to show off and they're sterile. Maybe I'm being a bit simplistic, but this was really the defining culture that seperated Fianna from other tribes, beyond the celtic hat. Werewolves that pay slightly more attention to nature... they all care about nature, what's exciting about a gardener that takes his job slightly more seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T03:49:07-07:00","id":1511338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511303#post1511303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing. But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them. Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how any of that works in setting, though. Spirits (and Falcon itself) are the arbiters of pure breed, not genetics or skin color. We know for a fact that there are groups of asian, african and arabic groups of Silver Fangs in addition to the ones descended from nobility of Europe.<br /> <br /> As for them denying good leaders, sure it's their problem, but at the end of day that's how you get Shadow Lords.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T04:00:20-07:00","id":1511339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511335#post1511335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's a fundamental misunderstanding of Stag's symbolism here, at least insofar as it was used by the Fianna. Fianna were always the party tribe who were boisterous, drunk, promiscuous and fond of telling tall tales to impress others. They were overly passionate. It made sense they followed stag, because that's kinda how Stags work. The defining feature of stags are the antlers, and they get big impressive antlers to impress the ladies and intimidate others, they wrestle other stags, the winner gets mating rights. That's Fianna life in a nutshell. Oh sure they adhere to the idea of being honourably mated but if that worked in practice they wouldn't be making so many metis. Maybe the reason they hated metis so much is because they're not good to show off and they're sterile. Maybe I'm being a bit simplistic, but this was really the defining culture that seperated Fianna from other tribes, beyond the celtic hat. Werewolves that pay slightly more attention to nature... they all care about nature, what's exciting about a gardener that takes his job slightly more seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely something to mention here, with the focus on the Tribes as mystery cults the identity and the narrative of the Totems are crucial. By stepping away from Stag as the embodiment of strength, showmanship and virility we should get a clear idea of what Stag actually represents and wants, there isn't really information about this nor what its agenda and purview may be. This general idea of hospitality and nurture is a weird choice and would need to be supported by a strong writeup of the totem and its themes and needs. We don't have that, nor does it seem to come through in this description of the tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T04:15:22-07:00","id":1511340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511339#post1511339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is definitely something to mention here, with the focus on the Tribes as mystery cults the identity and the narrative of the Totems are crucial. By stepping away from Stag as the embodiment of strength, showmanship and virility we should get a clear idea of what Stag actually represents and wants, there isn't really information about this nor what its agenda and purview may be. This general idea of hospitality and nurture is a weird choice and would need to be supported by a strong writeup of the totem and its themes and needs. We don't have that, nor does it seem to come through in this description of the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that regard, it also feels weird that despite still briefly mentioning the Hart Wardens love for Galliards and &quot;telling tall tales&quot;, Moots never come up in the write-up. Once again the whole communal aspect isn't really covered here. Really, the idea of &quot;Garou as a community&quot; in all the previews thus far only comes up so that it can be pointed out how divided Garou are and how they don't like each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T04:30:26-07:00","id":1511342,"title":"","content":"I will accept Asian silver fangs, but African silver fangs? Like, white-african silver fangs? Like the tribe's whole deal is how exclusive and inbred they are, and how impeccably white their coats are. Being exclusive snobs obsessed with purity to the point of rejecting someone with less than 3 pure breed is their human half when 2 is very good in most tribes and their wolf half is all about being white so you don't stick out in the snows of the far north where silver fangs hail from. There are no grey wolves in africa so there's no...<br /> <br /> What kind of overcompensation lead to this decision? Tribes aren't meant to be perfect and they all have pros and cons and characters aren't and don't need to be a reflection of the people who play them: I will happily play a woman to get into the black furies and I'll happily play a ginger to get into the Fianna... or a rich man to get into the glass walkers for that matter. A tribe being exclusive doesn't mean they're racist and going to relish in hate crimes against specific human populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-11-2023, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T05:07:56-07:00","id":1511344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511342#post1511342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will accept Asian silver fangs, but African silver fangs? Like, white-african silver fangs? Like the tribe's whole deal is how exclusive and inbred they are, and how impeccably white their coats are. Being exclusive snobs obsessed with purity to the point of rejecting someone with less than 3 pure breed is their human half when 2 is very good in most tribes and their wolf half is all about being white so you don't stick out in the snows of the far north where silver fangs hail from. There are no grey wolves in africa so there's no...<br /> <br /> What kind of overcompensation lead to this decision? Tribes aren't meant to be perfect and they all have pros and cons and characters aren't and don't need to be a reflection of the people who play them: I will happily play a woman to get into the black furies and I'll happily play a ginger to get into the Fianna... or a rich man to get into the glass walkers for that matter. A tribe being exclusive doesn't mean they're racist and going to relish in hate crimes against specific human populations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about nobility. And nobility existed all over the globe. An Arabian prince is as good as a Hindu Mughal or the Agongs of Malaysia. And it's not like you need wolves to have Garou somewhere in the world, majority of Garou are homid in the modern days.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T05:20:04-07:00","id":1511345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511342#post1511342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will accept Asian silver fangs, but African silver fangs? Like, white-african silver fangs? Like the tribe's whole deal is how exclusive and inbred they are, and how impeccably white their coats are. Being exclusive snobs obsessed with purity to the point of rejecting someone with less than 3 pure breed is their human half when 2 is very good in most tribes and their wolf half is all about being white so you don't stick out in the snows of the far north where silver fangs hail from. There are no grey wolves in africa so there's no...</div> </div> </div> </div>OK so...<br /> <br /> Whether you accept things or not doesn't really matter to what the books say. House Blood Red Crest is based in the Indian sub-continent, and House Wise Heart was originally based in the Fertile Crescent and has followed the expansion of Islamic royalty from the Balkans to Morocco. One of the things the other Tribes hate about the (at least pre-W5) Silver Fangs is that they used to come in and claim the best kin as theirs by right of being the highest of station, allowing them to take over royal/noble/etc. bloodlines across the world. While most of the surviving Houses in the modern nights are based in European ancestries, and European royal norms dominate their traditionalists for it, the wider Tribe is snobby and elitist by whatever the local standards are.<br /> <br /> Also remember that there's no way to see how many dots of Pure Breed a character has, and Falcon, not the Garou, sets the bar for how well bred a character has to be to get in. <br /> <br /> The coat colors of the Tribes has nothing to do with biology and is pure symbolism. The Shadow Lords, Silent Striders, and Black Furies are both noted for having dark black fur, something that only happens when domesticated dogs are mixed back into wild wold populations. Wild wolf populations don't have enough variations for 13 Tribes to all look different in their wolf forms (at least not in a fashion that's functional for a game where everyone hasn't memorized the differences between all the different <i>Canis lupus</i> subspecies}.<br /> <br /> And, while still rather debated how to classify it specifically, genetic analysis of the Egyptian jackal says it's either a subspecies of the grey wolf, or a second unique wolf species along with the Ethiopian wolf. This species is also considered misnamed since it's former range included all of Africa bordering the Sahara, including south. There is zero reason (other than the original books being written without access to information) why the Silver Fangs wouldn't have spread to the Ethiopian and west African empires just like they did into Asia: there's wolves there (and actual wolves, even if they're not grey wolves), and royalty there. The Silver Fangs didn't wait for white people to colonize the Middle East or India before setting up shop in those areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T06:56:47-07:00","id":1511349,"title":"","content":"As Heavy Arms said well above, pure breed is not race. Though it is sadly assumed by most, you can in fact have purebreed and be another race than where the tribe is originally from.<br /> <br /> With Hart Wardens, the Celts were not JUST Irish. As anyone with some knowledge of European comics knows, they were pretty established in France.<br /> <br /> While the WtA tribes are not as global as the Forsaken ones, one has to consider just how much travel and trade has happened over the millennia and finding tribes all over isn't that strange.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, the Get of Fenris might be anti-Viking, but their kin still travelled far and wide. We are talking about Africa and the Middle East up to North America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:06:23-07:00","id":1511350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511349#post1511349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Hart Wardens, the Celts were not JUST Irish. As anyone with some knowledge of European comics knows, they were pretty established in France.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Spain, and central Europe, even Turkey. They got around. People underestimate what a broad culture it was and how much land it covered and how far those people spread across the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 05-14-2023, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:10:15-07:00","id":1511351,"title":"","content":"Alright, even if I think you're selling black wolves short as they were considered relatively common in southern europe historically, I'll concede on coat colour as a magic symbolism thing and with that in mind silver fangs getting involved with west Asia, south asia and north africa is only natural (well, natural insofar as incestuous blue bloods go) <br /> <br /> However, concerning sub-saharan garou...<br /> 1- It's pretty established in canon that Hyenas and hunting dogs took up the spot because regular Garou couldn't<br /> 2-The wolves of Sub-Saharan africa are very small. <br /> 3- Given the relative remoteness from eurasia you'd think they'd have made their own tribes. <br /> 4- Africa presumably had wars of rage, and it doesn't look like the Garou won there. Intense competition from the other Fera. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also to me it never made sense that most tribes were bound to a culture or geography but silver fangs could somehow spread out and snag up all the royalty and leadership possitions without getting their royal asses handed to them. The idea to put them in russia/the north of eurasia made a good bit of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:12:58-07:00","id":1511352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511350#post1511350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Spain, and central Europe, even Turkey. They got around. People underestimate what a broad culture it was and how much land it covered and how far those people spread across the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I as a multi-generational citizen of my country (which was not even a country until 1918 and my roots go far longer than that) have German, Italian, English, Russian, Swedish and I'm sure more in my ancestry. Most of those are pre-18th century too.<br /> <br /> People travelled a LOT, as such you CAN have an Italian Strider, a Russian Fury and an Iranian Fenrir. It is just up to the players and the ST to understand that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:20:00-07:00","id":1511353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511262#post1511262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably because the Fianna were intimately tied with Celtic culture and the Hart Wardens are pan cultural . I have my reservations against a few of the separations of Garou tribes from human cultures but at the very least anyone can join any tribe.<br /> I totally get it that you guys are not feeling it though</div> </div> </div> </div>This was already possible way before W5 came about though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:33:49-07:00","id":1511356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511303#post1511303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing. But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them. Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed is also a spiritual thing. You could very well have a brazilian Silver Fang, not even related by blood to any noble line. Falcon would accept them just through their honor and how much they value the lessons given by the mottled mongrel becoming the White Wolf at the World's Navel to rescue Gaia from Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T07:39:10-07:00","id":1511357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511279#post1511279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Most tribes will take anyone in as long as they are willing to work within the tribal strictures and are accepted by the totem. The only tribe that had an ethnic filter of who could join was Wendigo - who were strictly no people who aren't Native American (well and Red Talons, but that's something else). All the tribal cultures had certain preferences and their cultures took from certain human cultures, but there were no limitations to who could join based on their ethnicity.<br /> <br /> Also, what is a Celt in the 21st Century anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>And even that Wendigo bloodline factor could be thought over with more details. Their TB Revised mentions how they don't deal in halves and how there are a lot of red skins but with white souls out there, abandoning the Old Gaian Way. They associate the white color with disdain to the Old Gaian Way (which is racist, no questions about it). If a white person would show loyalty to the Old Gaian Way, as their tribal Lodges and Hoops try to teach, I can see a rich plot of a white person being accepted by Great Wendigo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:10:32-07:00","id":1511358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511357#post1511357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And even that Wendigo bloodline factor could be thought over with more details. Their TB Revised mentions how they don't deal in halves and how there are a lot of red skins but with white souls out there, abandoning the Old Gaian Way. They associate the white color with disdain to the Old Gaian Way (which is racist, no questions about it). If a white person would show loyalty to the Old Gaian Way, as their tribal Lodges and Hoops try to teach, I can see a rich plot of a white person being accepted by Great Wendigo.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who lives and works among Native Americans (20 years of service to the tribe), that's really not how it works. They can respect me, but I'll never be able to join the tribe. You can rule stuff for your game, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:36:54-07:00","id":1511362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like it's worth noting that the Silver Fangs are also Ethnocentric, due to their bloodlines thing. <b>Yes, I'm aware that there are African Silver Fang bloodlines</b>, but picture the following scenario.<br /> <br /> A Homid cub from an impoverished background goes through their first change, and is rescued from the blood and red mist by a silver fang. This cub is a natural leader who has always been drawn towards ideas of justice, truth, making change through politics and so on, but also to chivalry and knighthood. They could be any race, but let's imagine for a moment they're black or latino. And as they go through all the explanations of what will happen next they tell this silver fang they wanna join their tribe, since they're so cool and just and devoted to this idea of rulership. It's what they were always meant to do.<br /> <br /> At which point they're told sorry, real sorry kid, but it's a select club. A... pure-breed having club. You need a certain kinda blood purity. <b>It's not a race thing! Definitely not a race thing.</b> But I, on odds a white dude given the Tribe's aristocratic roots, am now telling you that you can't join. But there are other valid tribes for you to join! Just not mine. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Soon after the silver fang, through dreams and omens, <b>comes to realize that this kid is in fact a long lost scion of an African or Spanish aristocratic line with blood ties to the Silver Fangs, and they are in fact suitably thick-blooded for Falcon to accept them.</b> Not because of any change in this person's behaviour or aptitude, but because of a realization regarding their heritage and their heritage alone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, thanks but fuck no. No I think I'd rather join one of the other tribes now. I'm actually kinda shocked you even reached out.&quot;<br /> <br /> The point of this isn't to say &quot;hereditary blood purity divine right monarchy is bad&quot; (I'm reasonably assuming you're all on the same page as me there), it's more to say &quot;<b>this tribe's obsession with blood purity will inevitably come off as racist, even if the Tribe isn't all-white&quot;</b>. </div> </div> </div>\u200bI kinda feel compelled to just quote my original post again. Went out of my way to acknowledge that Silver Fang lineages of all human ethnicities exist.<br /> <br /> The problem outlined in this scenario is one in which an arbitrary quality, who you are descended from, becomes pivotal to whether you are accepted into a Tribe which is meant to be the legitimate rulership of all Garou according to some sources. Pure Breed has some messy qualities going on, it can surprise you, people can pop up with a surprisingly strong spiritual connection to a very obscure blood tie which is either very difficult or impossible to nail down, but Silver Fangs do need to have PB of 3 or higher to join the Tribe at all.<br /> <br /> There being Black/Latino silver fangs is cold comfort to the kid described in my original post. Is he supposed to go &quot;wow I love that for them, I love how aristocrats with the same skin colour as me get to join your tribe&quot;. Is he supposed to go &quot;wow so it turns out my blood IS pure enough? Sign me up! I'm now fully on board again!&quot; No, neither of those things are gonna happen.<br /> <br /> Officially endorsing, no mandating, blood purity is going to wind up with your Tribe being tied to ideas of ethnocentrism, discrimination and inequality.<br /> <br /> And that's the point.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs are a Tribe of decadent nobles who believe that blood purity is an essential component to rulership, to leadership, to having the right to rule the Garou Nation. This makes them one of the more morally dubious or immoral tribes by default, from a perspective of human ethics.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;you don't need blood ties of any kind, Falcon can just decide you're a cool dude!&quot; - if your ST runs pure breed like that at your table, grand, but that isn't how it's written. If Falcon were liable to slap a magical PB3 onto anyone who is suitable to join the Tribe, the Tribe would look very different. Silver Fangs resort to marrying their aunts in their Revised Tribebook to maintain the necessary purity to qualify for the Tribe! Do you think they'd be doing that if they could just petition Falcon to fudge the numbers a bit on their PB 1-2 kids and bump them up a class?<br /> <br /> And yes when this is brought up a whole list of Silver Fang groups comes up who, as I acknowledge in my post, aren't white. But ultimately it isn't about race, it's about a pseudo-racial quality which we don't quite have an analogue for as humans. You could say it's an issue of class, if class were 100% hereditary. The discrimination at play here is quite vicious and dehumanizing, and undercuts the very idea of being a Tribe of worthy rulers, as some of the worthiest rulers are excluded from birth. Whether the person doing it has white skin or not almost becomes incidental; it only serves to deepen uncomfortable situations like the one I outlined above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:42:46-07:00","id":1511363,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a><br /> <br /> While people getting Pure Breed randomly slapped on is not really a thing, you might have pure breed from being offspring of Kinfolk or having a Garou in your relativley recent bloodline. Also there's no requirement to have &quot;Silver Fang Pure Breed&quot;. The Silver Fangs are well known for snapping up kinfolk no matter where they would belong family-wise.<br /> <br /> And again, your whole scenario is completely moot, as Pure Breed either is there or isn't. And it's not Garou who are arbiters of it - it's the spirits. Heck, it's Falcon that mandates Pure Breed 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:45:39-07:00","id":1511364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511362#post1511362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;you don't need blood ties of any kind, Falcon can just decide you're a cool dude!&quot; - if your ST runs pure breed like that at your table, grand, but that isn't how it's written. If Falcon were liable to slap a magical PB3 onto anyone who is suitable to join the Tribe, the Tribe would look very different. Silver Fangs resort to marrying their aunts in their Revised Tribebook to maintain the necessary purity to qualify for the Tribe! Do you think they'd be doing that if they could just petition Falcon to fudge the numbers a bit on their PB 1-2 kids and bump them up a class?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how pure breed works in W20 core. It CAN be a lineage you can recite, or it can just pop up randomly generations later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 Core p.138</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many werewolves with Pure Breed can trace their ancestry directly, while others resemble distant ancestors who cannot be connected without a degree of genealogical exactitude that is lost to the Garou.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also how the BSD PB5 thing works, they just randomly pop out a PB5 Howler but it means little as Lion is no longer their totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:53:15-07:00","id":1511366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511363#post1511363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a><br /> <br /> While people getting Pure Breed randomly slapped on is not really a thing, you might have pure breed from being offspring of Kinfolk or having a Garou in your relativley recent bloodline. Also there's no requirement to have &quot;Silver Fang Pure Breed&quot;. The Silver Fangs are well known for snapping up kinfolk no matter where they would belong family-wise.<br /> <br /> And again, your whole scenario is completely moot, as Pure Breed either is there or isn't. And it's not Garou who are arbiters of it - it's the spirits. Heck, it's Falcon that mandates Pure Breed 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed is tribe-specific as per W20 - a male child of Black Furies might have a PB 5 Black Fury mother and a PB5 Black Fury Kinfolk father, say, but will have PB0 in any other tribe.<br /> <br /> <i>Pure Breed is a nebulous combination of bloodline and spiritual inheritance. A character with high Pure Breed looks and carries himself like an archetypal member of his tribe \u2014 <b>however, if he does not join that tribe, any benefits of Pure Breed are removed by the tribe\u2019s totem.</b></i><br /> <br /> Silver Fangs snapping up Purebred Kinfolk of other tribes is a thing, and people explain it one of two ways; Kinfolk are eligible to pass on pure breed well regardless of what tribe it's tied to, since their pure breed is not the same Background as Garou's (they just share a name etc.), or positing that the Silver Fangs have some method of bridging the gap. I go for the former as there's no canon hint of the latter.<br /> <br /> The scenario I present is one in which a cub is mistaken for not having the necessary pure breed, but is later discovered to be eligible by the mandate of spirits.<br /> <br /> Garou aren't the arbitrators of whether Pure Breed is present, no, but if you simply shift the blame upwards to Falcon you end up with a situation of:<br /> <br /> - if this Totem is so awful, why is he qualified to represent the Tribe who are meant to rule?<br /> - are the Silver Fangs just passive prisoners in this situation? are they doing everything they can to petition Falcon to lower the PB requirement to 2 or 1?<br /> - if it's impossible to change such things, how did the Glass Walkers petition Cockroach to do away with Pure Breed in their Tribe, and how did the Black Furies convince Pegasus to allow their male Metis cubs to join the tribe?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the Silver Fangs are uniquely monstrous or evil, but they're deeply flawed in interesting ways. I like it when this is engaged with! It can make for compelling stories! Garou who were sufficiently pure blooded to join the Silver Fangs but rejected the Tribe because they think hereditary monarchy is bad. Modernizers who try, as some canon Silver Fangs have, to push the Tribe more towards believing in the ideals of rulership as opposed to inheritance of divine right. What happens when Fangs try to popularize the idea of allowing any trace of SF ancestry, no matter how faint, to qualify? Who fights back against this idea? Can Falcon be convinced? What would it take to prove the idea to him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:56:28-07:00","id":1511367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511364#post1511364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is how pure breed works in W20 core. It CAN be a lineage you can recite, or it can just pop up randomly generations later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I'm aware. Like I say PB is nebulous, it can defy expectations, it can confound attempts to explain it. It's a mixture of genealogy and spiritual inheritance. This doesn't mean that any Garou who is destined to be an incredible ruler, the kind who would exemplify what it means to be a silver fang (at their best) gets PB3 for that Tribe. Basically PB can behave in weird or unexpected ways, but I'll narrow my eyes if I see someone citing that as a way to try and wash the Silver Fangs clean - just because the spirits sometimes behave in weird ways doesn't mean that a system that values blood purity suddenly becomes okay; after all if the silver fangs just went &quot;PB does whatever, man, ya know?&quot; they'd probably stop fighting so hard to manage their bloodlines to ensure ongoing purity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T08:58:54-07:00","id":1511368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511358#post1511358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who lives and works among Native Americans (20 years of service to the tribe), that's really not how it works. They can respect me, but I'll never be able to join the tribe. You can rule stuff for your game, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is how it work in real life.<br /> wta is not real life. There are examples of wendigo even in Africa and even &quot;exceptions always exists&quot; in kinfolk 20pth<br /> <br /> Dont want to be rude or sounds like the hateful teacher. Just adding details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:02:13-07:00","id":1511369,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth noting that Younger Brother has adopted indigenous people of all kinds into their tribe - it isn't &quot;you have to be Native American&quot;, it's &quot;you can't be a Wyrmbringer&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:07:30-07:00","id":1511370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511367#post1511367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, I'm aware. Like I say PB is nebulous, it can defy expectations, it can confound attempts to explain it. It's a mixture of genealogy and spiritual inheritance. This doesn't mean that any Garou who is destined to be an incredible ruler, the kind who would exemplify what it means to be a silver fang (at their best) gets PB3 for that Tribe. Basically PB can behave in weird or unexpected ways, but I'll narrow my eyes if I see someone citing that as a way to try and wash the Silver Fangs clean - just because the spirits sometimes behave in weird ways doesn't mean that a system that values blood purity suddenly becomes okay; after all if the silver fangs just went &quot;PB does whatever, man, ya know?&quot; they'd probably stop fighting so hard to manage their bloodlines to ensure ongoing purity!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It isn't an effort to wash the Fangs clean, just that PB isn't tied to one race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:09:50-07:00","id":1511371,"title":"","content":"BTW I think it's interesting to look at the description of PB 2, which has some neat flavour text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your grandfather made a name for himself at the Battle of Bloody Ford, and you carry that name with pride. </div> </div> </div>What's interesting about this is that the Silver Fang requirement isn't &quot;has PB&quot;, it's &quot;has PB3+&quot;. And you're left to wonder at what point is that enforced.<br /> <br /> A Garou who discovers a cub who is a grandchild of a Silver Fang of some note, for instance, might well think &quot;well he's tied to the Silver Fangs by blood, the spirits will accept him&quot;. And even if people can sense the Pure Breed of cubs, &quot;feel&quot; it (which seems reasonable), they won't be able to accurately distinguish PB2 from PB3.<br /> <br /> So when do you actually get rejected?<br /> <br /> It seems most likely, that in a tragic case like this, you'd be rejected at the moment of your Rite of Initiation. Which is pretty heartbreaking. No intervention, no argument, no test, no proof of your honour and dignity, no victory, nothing will ever prove that you're worthy of Falcon. Best be on your way, to join a tribe in which your PB2 will disappear off your &quot;sheet&quot; as it were.<br /> <br /> The narrative space for &quot;embittered Garou who didn't get to utilize their SF PB b/c it was 1 or 2&quot; or &quot;embittered Garou who didn't get to utilize their BF PB b/c they're a man&quot; is pretty intriguing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:10:21-07:00","id":1511372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511370#post1511370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It isn't an effort to wash the Fangs clean, just that PB isn't tied to one race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah we're agreed there - Pure Breed isn't tied to one race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:13:32-07:00","id":1511373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511366#post1511366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pure Breed is tribe-specific as per W20 - a male child of Black Furies might have a PB 5 Black Fury mother and a PB5 Black Fury Kinfolk father, say, but will have PB0 in any other tribe.<br /> <br /> <i>Pure Breed is a nebulous combination of bloodline and spiritual inheritance. A character with high Pure Breed looks and carries himself like an archetypal member of his tribe \u2014 <b>however, if he does not join that tribe, any benefits of Pure Breed are removed by the tribe\u2019s totem.</b></i><br /> <br /> Silver Fangs snapping up Purebred Kinfolk of other tribes is a thing, and people explain it one of two ways; Kinfolk are eligible to pass on pure breed well regardless of what tribe it's tied to, since their pure breed is not the same Background as Garou's (they just share a name etc.), or positing that the Silver Fangs have some method of bridging the gap. I go for the former as there's no canon hint of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Considering how messy W20 is and how much it copy pastes things in one place and then changes something in another I think they conflated two different rules into one. You lose Pure Breed if you switch tribes, but it's not tribe specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511366#post1511366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scenario I present is one in which a cub is mistaken for not having the necessary pure breed, but is later discovered to be eligible by the mandate of spirits.<br /> \u200b<br /> Garou aren't the arbitrators of whether Pure Breed is present, no, but if you simply shift the blame upwards to Falcon you end up with a situation of:<br /> <br /> - if this Totem is so awful, why is he qualified to represent the Tribe who are meant to rule?<br /> - are the Silver Fangs just passive prisoners in this situation? are they doing everything they can to petition Falcon to lower the PB requirement to 2 or 1?<br /> - if it's impossible to change such things, how did the Glass Walkers petition Cockroach to do away with Pure Breed in their Tribe, and how did the Black Furies convince Pegasus to allow their male Metis cubs to join the tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are either eligible or you're not. This is not something that's impossible to figure out or mystically invisible. If you had applied for membership you would have passed then and there. If not you would have had a different life and a suspiciously silver-white fur among the Black Furies or Fianna.<br /> <br /> This isn't about the blame. Silver Fangs are stuck up elitists, that's a given. Falcon is a stuck up elitist, that's also given. However, any assumption that Silver Fangs are this tightly defined group of European nobles is pure poppycock. As far as your ethnicity goes you're not going to be in problems. The question is do you belong to the right families and do you have the mystic oomph in your bloodline as recognised by the Totem of the Fangs.<br /> <br /> I don't think the totem is awful. It is what it is. They are as proud of it as it is of itself. You're being obtuse here by insisting that this is a problem. The Elitism is a part of Fang culture and of who they and their totem are. According the to Silver Record they were chosen for this role and blessed to be the annointed Kings. This is not a problem for the game itself but can be an interesting source of backstory and tensions. And your other examples are sillyness - it's not the tribe that makes the Totem, it's the Totem that makes the tribe. Cockroach and Rat are the lowest of the low and hell bent to survive any possible situation, what would they care where you came from?<br /> <br /> Is it that hard to realise that Silver Fangs are supposed to all about a downright medieval and Arthurian concept of Once and Future Kings? That's who they are for better or for worse. What<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511366#post1511366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying the Silver Fangs are uniquely monstrous or evil, but they're deeply flawed in interesting ways. I like it when this is engaged with! It can make for compelling stories! Garou who were sufficiently pure blooded to join the Silver Fangs but rejected the Tribe because they think hereditary monarchy is bad. Modernizers who try, as some canon Silver Fangs have, to push the Tribe more towards believing in the ideals of rulership as opposed to inheritance of divine right. What happens when Fangs try to popularize the idea of allowing any trace of SF ancestry, no matter how faint, to qualify? Who fights back against this idea? Can Falcon be convinced? What would it take to prove the idea to him?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're so hell bent on enforcing your concept of the misidentified poorly judged leader that you're missing the point that noone is arguing that Fangs can be (and often are) assholes. We are arguing that ethnicity and geography aren't blocking you from joining up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:20:19-07:00","id":1511374,"title":"","content":"You've definitely misread my original post, but that's okay - I get the feeling we generally agree but are coming at it from a different angle. Like I said in my original post there are SF houses/bloodlines/individuals of all human ethnicities, and the tribe isn't stuck to one geography/race.<br /> <br /> Claiming that a rule in the book is a mistake or copy+pasted incorrectly, or is meant to say something different to what it says... I mean that's possible, I can't prove a negative on that, but you could say that of any rule. IMO it's pretty clear that PB is tribe specific in W20, but people can run it as they like at their table; it's probably one of the things that varies most from table to table tbh.<br /> <br /> I really don't want to keep having to refer back to my original post and keep having to say &quot;yeah, I didn't say that&quot; in response to various posts so ngl I'm not getting much out of this convo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-11-2023, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:42:10-07:00","id":1511375,"title":"","content":".......bit bland innit?<br /> <br /> Plus as a celt im not happy at celtic erasure in general when you could just make them not alcoholics and ira.<br /> <br /> Are these even the fianna in any meaningful sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T09:44:10-07:00","id":1511376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511375#post1511375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.......bit bland innit?<br /> <br /> Plus as a celt im not happy at celtic erasure in general when you could just make them not alcoholics and ira.<br /> <br /> Are these even the fianna in any meaningful sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they guard places tied to nature, which is lovely and specific. We all know the other Tribes don't have any patience for guarding sacred places deep in the wilderness!<br /> <br /> A friend of mine read the preview and immediately went:<br /> <br /> &quot;It's like if you did a Toreador write-up, and their unique selling point were &quot;the Toreador feed upon the blood of mortals to survive&quot;, or a Satyr write-up which said &quot;Satyr are fae souls bound into human bodies&quot;, or a Hermetic write-up which said &quot;Hermetics use their Practice to manipulate reality&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:02:12-07:00","id":1511377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511376#post1511376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well they guard places tied to nature, which is lovely and specific. We all know the other Tribes don't have any patience for guarding sacred places deep in the wilderness!<br /> <br /> A friend of mine read the preview and immediately went:<br /> <br /> &quot;It's like if you did a Toreador write-up, and their unique selling point were &quot;the Toreador feed upon the blood of mortals to survive&quot;, or a Satyr write-up which said &quot;Satyr are fae souls bound into human bodies&quot;, or a Hermetic write-up which said &quot;Hermetics use their Practice to manipulate reality&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that more of what's make each tribe unique is spread throughout the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:05:07-07:00","id":1511378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511376#post1511376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well they guard places tied to nature, which is lovely and specific. We all know the other Tribes don't have any patience for guarding sacred places deep in the wilderness!<br /> <br /> A friend of mine read the preview and immediately went:<br /> <br /> &quot;It's like if you did a Toreador write-up, and their unique selling point were &quot;the Toreador feed upon the blood of mortals to survive&quot;, or a Satyr write-up which said &quot;Satyr are fae souls bound into human bodies&quot;, or a Hermetic write-up which said &quot;Hermetics use their Practice to manipulate reality&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair v5 lasombra are a group of shadowy manipulative predators in a species of shadowy manipulative predators","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:13:40-07:00","id":1511379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511377#post1511377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that more of what's make each tribe unique is spread throughout the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, but you can see why people would expect the Tribe's uniqueness to be sold to you in the core &quot;pitch&quot; of their writeup. I mean this section was chosen for a preview for a reason! If the Tribe's identity is elsewhere, show that bit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:23:45-07:00","id":1511382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511377#post1511377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that more of what's make each tribe unique is spread throughout the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's true but even in the case that it is if I were to review the book this exact same sentiment would land in the Negatives-section for me. This is a <i>terrible </i>way to structure a corebook. Having to hunt for details on player-options across multiple pages in different sections of the corebook is bad. You're creating unnecessary extra work for potential STs and/or players by doing that. The point of these typical WOD-factions presentations is to give you the gist of what that faction is about. If those two pages don't do that... what was the point of it in the first place...? That's why this sentiment you expressed is purely a critique in my opinion. What you're describing is a bad thing, something a Corebook should <i>not </i>do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:23:50-07:00","id":1511383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511302#post1511302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that WtA treated Tribal weaknesses as optional (mostly because Pack Totems have them too). But since I didn't notice someone addressing this part:<br /> <br /> The old Fianna Weakness was +1 difficulty on Willpower rolls to represent the Tribe's penchant for passion and poor self-control.<br /> <br /> Stag's Ban as a pack Totem was that followers of Stag had to answer any request from aid from fae creatures or spirits, as well as always having to perform the Prayer for the Prey rite to the spirit of their kills after any hunt they participated in.<br /> <br /> So the concept of making their Tribal restriction a more generalized hospitality thing isn't a huge departure from previous material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, what is the restriction for being a Fianna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T11:06:21-07:00","id":1511389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511383#post1511383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant, what is the restriction for being a Fianna?</div> </div> </div> </div>?<br /> <br /> Its in the post that you quoted if you mean the optional Tribal Flaw, if your asking if there are any restrictions on who can become Fianna? Nope, as long as Stag says yes they're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T11:34:32-07:00","id":1511393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511351#post1511351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, even if I think you're selling black wolves short as they were considered relatively common in southern europe historically...,</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no pure wild type &quot;black&quot; wolves. &quot;Black wolves&quot; in southern Europe were either mixed with melanistic dogs (all black, no discernible pattern), or were just dark grey wolves (which is common in the Eurasian wolf) that lacked the &quot;red&quot; color in their fur but still have gradients of white and black to form the coat patterns of wild wolves. Wolf and dog mixing in Europe is not some recent phenomenon, it just clashes with the idea that there would be Tribes where melanistic coats are a sign of high breeding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (well, natural insofar as incestuous blue bloods go) </div> </div> </div>The incestuous part hasn't been canon since 1e. 2e just used the already small breeding pool of European nobles to paint the Tribe that way (neglecting that four main Houses explicitly didn't abide by such), and Rev/20 both dropped that part completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3- Given the relative remoteness from eurasia you'd think they'd have made their own tribes. </div> </div> </div>Um, what relative remoteness? The western African empires and the Ethiopian empires all had active trading routes that extended to Eurasia. I think you're forgetting how big Africa is, as the Western empires were all closer, geographically to Europe than they were to the southern end of Africa. Benin is closer to Spain, than Portugal is to the main territory of Russia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea to put them in russia/the north of eurasia made a good bit of sense. </div> </div> </div>That's never what the books did though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511366#post1511366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed is tribe-specific as per W20 - a male child of Black Furies might have a PB 5 Black Fury mother and a PB5 Black Fury Kinfolk father, say, but will have PB0 in any other tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed isn't Tribe specific for Kinfolk. Even with the citation of the book, Kin can't join Tribes, so either their PB can never matter, or it can't be a Tribe-specific thing (which was more explicit in previous editions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I go for the former as there's no canon hint of the latter. </div> </div> </div>No W20 != no canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if it's impossible to change such things, how did the Glass Walkers petition Cockroach to do away with Pure Breed in their Tribe, and how did the Black Furies convince Pegasus to allow their male Metis cubs to join the tribe? </div> </div> </div>Where did either of these events happen?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511383#post1511383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant, what is the restriction for being a Fianna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Convincing a Fianna to do the Rite, and Stag saying yes.<br /> <br /> Pre-W5, only three Tribes had &quot;restrictions&quot; about things beyond individual decisions: Silver Fangs (PB 3+), Black Furies (no male homids and lupus), and Red Talons (no homids).<br /> <br /> Every other Tribe was up to the petitioning Cub, the Tribe's person with the Rite to ask their Totem spirit, and the Totem spirit on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> Evan Heals the Past made it into Younger Brother, despite Younger Brother's Garou general not liking white people. Even in Tribes like Younger Brother or the Get of Fenris that tend to be very picky about certain things, there's usually a Ragabash around willing to risk pissing off some spirits to challenge their Tribes preconceptions about who makes for a proper member of their Tribe according to the spirits if the Garou would give them a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T12:47:57-07:00","id":1511397,"title":"","content":"Took another look - says that the Glass Walkers simply &quot;stopped cultivating&quot; their PB, so Cockroach wasn't involved.<br /> <br /> As for the Black Furies, they used to not accept their own male Metis. W20's Umbra book details that since they started accepting male metis, emanations of boys and men have begun to appear in the Black Fury Spiritual Homeland, where previously there were only women and girls. It's also said that Pegasus refuses to accept males, with the exception of metis offspring of the Black Furies (the new status quo). At some point there was a changeover:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another major shift is the presence of men in the homeland. The Furies permitted no males in the Realm until recently; they relaxed the ban for their male Metis children. This unexpectedly led to greater changes \u2014 Furies suddenly found men in the human settlements where previously there were none. </div> </div> </div>Either Pegasus changed her mind and told the Tribe to start adopting Metis, or the Black Furies reached a consensus of adopting Metis and petitioned Pegasus to accept these children of theirs. Either is plausible, but the latter is implied I would argue, as it says &quot;they&quot; relaxed the ban.<br /> <br /> And yeah, like I said PB is tribe-specific, but Kinfolk don't seem to have tribe-specific PB (though W20 could be clearer about the latter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-11-2023, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:06:04-07:00","id":1511403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511358#post1511358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who lives and works among Native Americans (20 years of service to the tribe), that's really not how it works. They can respect me, but I'll never be able to join the tribe. You can rule stuff for your game, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not talking about a human tribe, I'm talking about a Garou tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:32:46-07:00","id":1511409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511397#post1511397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either Pegasus changed her mind and told the Tribe to start adopting Metis, or the Black Furies reached a consensus of adopting Metis and petitioned Pegasus to accept these children of theirs. Either is plausible, but the latter is implied I would argue, as it says &quot;they&quot; relaxed the ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, neither? Pegasus was always willing to accept male Metis, just for a long time the Black Furies refused to ask. Once it was made clear to the Black Furies that Pegasus would accept male Metis, their numbers grew in the Tribe.<br /> <br /> It's been the case since the first Black Fury TB that the Garou, not the spirits were responsible for this; not that Pegasus had a change of heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, like I said PB is tribe-specific, but Kinfolk don't seem to have tribe-specific PB (though W20 could be clearer about the latter). </div> </div> </div>You claimed a child of a PB 5 Black Fury and a PB 5 mate from a Black Fury background would result in a Garou child that would have PB 0 if they joined any other Tribe. This isn't supported as such by the text. It's likely, but nothing stops them from being a PB 1 or 2 Child of Gaia, there's intermarriage between Tribes, esp. with the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511403#post1511403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not talking about a human tribe, I'm talking about a Garou tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: Evan-Heals-the-Past made it into the Garou Tribe you're talking about. Shitty character aside, the books aren't as strict as you're making them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T15:21:07-07:00","id":1511414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511377#post1511377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that more of what's make each tribe unique is spread throughout the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know that? Did you actually see the rest of the book, or is this an act of blind Faith in the devs? Because I've seen their other work in Hunter, and the Creeds were exactly what was in their spreads and nothing more.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that these 2 page spreads were the sellers of the splats. They were the moneyshot of the book and it was where you kept going back towards an evocative image of the splats. For most folks it was what sold them onto their favourite splat and sang to them. Back in the day I first laid my eyes on Vampire you had a two page spread with one big impressive piece of art, the quotes about others that made their attitudes clear and a description bursting with flavour and mysteries that could inspire you to play with THIS group and no other.<br /> <br /> This is not a very good sell sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T16:32:41-07:00","id":1511416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511409#post1511409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again: Evan-Heals-the-Past made it into the Garou Tribe you're talking about. Shitty character aside, the books aren't as strict as you're making them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not arguing against that point. I was agreeing with you at that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T17:16:43-07:00","id":1511417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511414#post1511414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you know that? Did you actually see the rest of the book, or is this an act of blind Faith in the devs? Because I've seen their other work in Hunter, and the Creeds were exactly what was in their spreads and nothing more.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that these 2 page spreads were the sellers of the splats. They were the moneyshot of the book and it was where you kept going back towards an evocative image of the splats. For most folks it was what sold them onto their favourite splat and sang to them. Back in the day I first laid my eyes on Vampire you had a two page spread with one big impressive piece of art, the quotes about others that made their attitudes clear and a description bursting with flavour and mysteries that could inspire you to play with THIS group and no other.<br /> <br /> This is not a very good sell sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a comment on the Dev cycle,but you are right that i cannot know it for sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-11-2023, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T01:30:06-07:00","id":1511432,"title":"","content":"I am glad that W5 will have its fans, and rightly so. Werewolf is awesome! I'm glad new people will be brought in, and it may prove a gateway to W20 for those new players. I know a lot of V20 / &quot;20th&quot; players of all splats whose first ever WOD game was V5.<br /> <br /> At the same time I think it's worth acknowledging that the people writing the book aren't a reliable source on the quality of the book. It'd be weird if they didn't like or defend it!<br /> <br /> Controversies aside, negative comments on the work of old writers aside, half-truths and veiled insults aside, even when I ignore a plethora of reasons to write off W5, I find that the previews are just bleh. Having four sample characters is a cool idea, having four drawings for each Tribe is a cool idea!<br /> <br /> For instance looking at W20 I could easily imagine the Glass Walker we see with Cockroach in his shadow having a few companions; a slightly mangy Lupus with a cybernetic jaw, a Crinos holding a cracked computer tablet and a gun, a Homid dressed for a business meeting with a wolf-like grin. And having writeups for who those four people are, their Auspices, how they fit into the Tribe, would be so cool! You could even shoot for a nice round five so as to give an example of each Auspice in each Tribe; it'd be word count and art intensive, but IMO it would be worth it.<br /> <br /> But as much as I like the concept of multiple characters, I just look at a lineup of photomanipulated-looking human-looking people who could easily be Mages or Vampires or Changelings for all I know, none of whom have roles which seem to require a giant war form to fulfil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T06:11:59-07:00","id":1511443,"title":"","content":"I don't think that people are complaining about the book because they just want to hate on something. Least, I like to think not. I think most complaints come from a place of wanting an amazing product. We talk about the things we don't like out of love of the setting and love of the game. Sometimes we so do passionately so it can come off as vitriolic. Sometime it is vitriolic.<br /> <br /> I have long since said that I'm not the target demographic for x5 lines and while I still stand by that statement I think this latest preview of what is my favorite tribe really cements it into my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T06:13:44-07:00","id":1511444,"title":"","content":"For me, the biggest issue remains the inconsistent writing. Because there ARE people who want to play WtA but DON'T want to learn all the Nation minutea or deal with the Curse making interacting with humans hard, these people are valid.<br /> <br /> But then last week we were told most werewolves CAN'T hack it among humans, only for the same preview to contradict itself with the Party Animal pack. Then the Hart Warden preview continues the trend by having only one archetype that mildly sounds like someone outside society.<br /> <br /> On top of this, the werewolf of the werewolf game is missing in the tribe previews.<br /> <br /> So currently W5 seems to be in a three-way tug-of-war with itself. Are the characters actually raging beasts or not? Can or can they not blend among humans? Are they fighting to lessen the Apocalypse or are they too busy filing taxes to do much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T11:12:58-07:00","id":1511461,"title":"","content":"Maybe the fact that you don't fit into human society that well but have to is meant to be the meat of the game. It's not really what the other preview information suggests, but it would very much be a valid game.<br /> <br /> Although it's more likely to be that the devs just didn't think about the disconnect between being the mildly successful owner of a secondhand bookstore in downtime and a volatile rage monster during playtime. That so much effort was put into creating that specific street level story that what comes before and after it is forgotten.<br /> <br /> As to the Hart Wardens, honestly the idea of them being a Tribe specifically dedicated to <i>cultivated nature</i> has legs to it, with them trying to balance the spread of cultivated land with the preservation of diverse ecosystems. I can see them in the wheat fields or woodlands at the dead of night drinking cider, singing bawdy songs, and boasting about how they've made farms more sustainable. It's a shame the developers apparently missed that idea to primarily focus on them doing the exact same thing as other Garou.<br /> <br /> But at least unlike with the Glass Walkers I'm not getting that much of a 'one note Forsaken Tribe' note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T12:03:00-07:00","id":1511467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511461#post1511461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Hart Wardens, honestly the idea of them being a Tribe specifically dedicated to <i>cultivated nature</i> has legs to it, with them trying to balance the spread of cultivated land with the preservation of diverse ecosystems. I can see them in the wheat fields or woodlands at the dead of night drinking cider, singing bawdy songs, and boasting about how they've made farms more sustainable. It's a shame the developers apparently missed that idea to primarily focus on them doing the exact same thing as other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would've been better, I think. I really like the idea of the new concept being all about making sure civilization and nature can live in harmony with each other and make that the animating idea of the Tribe in W5. And whereas the Hart Wardens are all about the harmony of the land/environment, you get other Tribes like Children of Gaia who focus on harmony amongst the people living on the land and the Ghost Council Tribe is about living in harmony with the spirit-world, for example. I'm just spitballing here but this is about setting up a new paradigm for why there are all these Tribes of Garou around.<br /> <br /> Instead, though, the concept they seemed to go for was to make them &quot;stewards of nature&quot; - but in a <i>very </i>broad sense. Both the people who want to preserve nature untouched by humanity and those who want to cultivate it in order to create farmland, for example, are somehow all part of this Tribe. And the storytelling-bit is way too prominent still, I feel like. This isn't supposed to be the Fianna of old, so I don't understand why the love for Galliards and &quot;tall tales&quot; is still there in the write-up. The only reason these elements are there is because the Hart Wardens are the W5-version of the Fianna of previous editions. The whole point of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; is to not be beholden to previous editions like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T12:52:18-07:00","id":1511472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511461#post1511461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the fact that you don't fit into human society that well but have to is meant to be the meat of the game. It's not really what the other preview information suggests, but it would very much be a valid game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? It would and it would actually be interesting to play out since there is no escape to nature. The garou just have to deal with humanity and grit their teeth.<br /> <br /> But I do feel the issue is that writers are writing past each other with no cohesive base.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T13:15:50-07:00","id":1511475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511472#post1511472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do feel the issue is that writers are writing past each other with no cohesive base.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I've never been a fan of throwing out a ton of lore while replacing it with nothing - while also keeping key-elements (like 11 Tribes). Trying to explain W5 is just a constant back-and-forth of explaining why it's the fifth edition of WtA and why it isn't like any of its previous editions.<br /> <br /> And one element, I'm still very wary of is the whole treatment of the Native American Tribes. Supposedly the principle is that all ties between human culture/ethnicities and Garou Tribes have been severed. But we've seen with Hart Wardens how there are still elements of the old Fianna in there for no other reason than this being a new version of that Tribe in previous editions. Now take that idea and imagine what could happen with the Tribes that used to be Native American ones. Old WtA certainly had its issues but this edition was supposedly all about doing better. And yet what we've learned thus far is that both the approach to changing things (which we got with the whole Fianna-thing) and a cultural sensitivity reader checking things (like the art in the GW-preview) turned out to be not very thorough. So in my mind, both the Galestalker and the Ghost Council write-ups are potential controversies to be triggered once the public gets a chance to read them. With all that we know now, how thorough do we think were the writers in distinguishing between referencing past lore of the Younger Brother and Elder Brother Tribe and referencing Native American traditions (and potentially doing so incorrectly)...?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T13:49:14-07:00","id":1511477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511475#post1511475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With all that we know now, how thorough do we think were the writers in distinguishing between referencing past lore of the Younger Brother and Elder Brother Tribe and referencing Native American traditions (and potentially doing so incorrectly)...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the treatment of James and some of Karims gauche statements in the past? Not bloody very.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T17:45:23-07:00","id":1511492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511477#post1511477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the treatment of James and some of Karims gauche statements in the past? Not bloody very.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did I miss now? Thought Karim was the quiet one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T21:26:13-07:00","id":1511503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511409#post1511409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: Evan-Heals-the-Past made it into the Garou Tribe you're talking about. Shitty character aside, the books aren't as strict as you're making them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evan is Native American. Not all Natives have darker skin and live on a rez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T23:53:29-07:00","id":1511509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511475#post1511475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I've never been a fan of throwing out a ton of lore while replacing it with nothing - while also keeping key-elements (like 11 Tribes). Trying to explain W5 is just a constant back-and-forth of explaining why it's the fifth edition of WtA and why it isn't like any of its previous editions.<br /> <br /> And one element, I'm still very wary of is the whole treatment of the Native American Tribes. Supposedly the principle is that all ties between human culture/ethnicities and Garou Tribes have been severed. But we've seen with Hart Wardens how there are still elements of the old Fianna in there for no other reason than this being a new version of that Tribe in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>as a celt (welsh/scottish)I can't see anything of my people in the Tribe. I don't consider the Hart wardens the fianna at all and theyre certainly not linked with me or mine. I can't speak for first nation peoples but I think they're going to achieve their objective. Which is ultimatly a shame imo since what it amounts to is the abandonment of one of the few first nation Canadian peoples in fiction because they didn't want to take a risk by trying to do it well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-13-2023, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:08:24-07:00","id":1511513,"title":"","content":"Evan is explicitly white (and supposedly the first white person to become a member of Younger Brother). While he might have native ancestry, he's not a recognized member of any tribe. Having some distant blood relatives doesn't make you automatically part of one. If even hadn't had his first change, he'd just be some boring white dude that probably wouldn't have even know his great-grandparent or something wasn't white unless he decided to do some genetic test for shits and giggles. If he didn't have Garou and Kin vouching for him, he'd never be allowed in Native spaces.<br /> <br /> I'm well aware that there are white-passing Native Americans that don't live on reservation, but there's a difference between growing up raised in a culture even if you don't look like what outsiders would think of, and finding out you're 1/16th or whatever and then trying to claim you're a member of that tribe/people. Evan is as much a Native American as Elizabeth Warren, he just exists in a world with spirits that are going around forcing Younger Brother to accept him as one of their own (which doesn't mean any human Native American tribe has actually done so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:52:29-07:00","id":1511518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511513#post1511513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and finding out you're 1/16th or whatever and then trying to claim you're a member of that tribe/people.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:blue\">Isn't that what Americans do anyway?</span><br /> <br /> But yes, I agree with your point. I'm not Irish, despite having grandparents from the RoI, and even if I got the documents together to become an Irish citizen I still wouldn't be culturally Irish. With historically persecuted cultures (like the Welsh) it's even more important to respect their interpretation of who is and isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> Plus Evan is one of the things I fairly regularly see cited as an issue with classic Werewolf. I really hope that if W5 has signature characters they manage to do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:09:58-07:00","id":1511520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511509#post1511509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> as a celt (welsh/scottish)I can't see anything of my people in the Tribe. I don't consider the Hart wardens the fianna at all and theyre certainly not linked with me or mine. I can't speak for first nation peoples but I think they're going to achieve their objective. Which is ultimatly a shame imo since what it amounts to is the abandonment of one of the few first nation Canadian peoples in fiction because they didn't want to take a risk by trying to do it well.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant is how the Hart Wardens description throws in the bit of them loving to be storytellers with the caveat that they also like to tell tall tales. This has nothing to do with the &quot;stewards of nature&quot;-concept and more to do with them being Fianna before. It's this haphazard process of having these bits of the old version still being in there. Like, in the previews it talked about how the Galestalker-Tribe's Ban is them having to partake in a fresh kill daily. If you know that this used to be the Younger Brother Tribe, it's a weird bit from the old version still being present there. But the point was to completely get away from this stuff. And what I'm worrying is that if they aren't thorough in really making sure the new versions of these Tribes are their own thing, something problematic might sneak into the writing like what happened with the Second Inquisition book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:19:40-07:00","id":1511521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511509#post1511509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> as a celt (welsh/scottish)I can't see anything of my people in the Tribe. I don't consider the Hart wardens the fianna at all and they're certainly not linked with me or mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, Werewolf is nowhere near my main, so there could be information I'm not aware of, but a name change is actually something I would've wanted for this reason.<br /> <i>Fianna</i>, as far as I've ever been able to find out, is specifically Gaelic and has nothing to do with the Brythonic Celts. It feels like another case of Americans deciding Celtic=Irish, then remembering Scotland as an afterthought. If you're lucky, they know that Wales is not actually interchangeable with England. Then Cornwall, Brittany and the Isle of Mann are met with &quot;???&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Fianna are the Celtic tribe, not just the Irish/Hibernian tribe, then they've got a name from a legend with zero connection to 4/6 (or 3/6, unsure about the Manx) of the Celtic cultures. I mean, as I said, maybe they do have other names tucked away in a tribe book I've never read, in which case I rescind my complaints. But while &quot;Hart Warden&quot; doesn't really tie into any of the other myths that I'm aware of, I'd rather have Welsh werewolves call themselves something like <i>y Ceidwad yr Hydd</i> than <i>Fianna/F\u00e8inne</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not happy with just slapping on a bland, meaningless name, but it'd do until I hunt down something Fianna-Cyclr-equivalent in the Mabinogion, or something.<br /> <br /> This is something of a moot point, because W5 has nothing to do with any of that, but at the very least I'm considering stealing the reboot name back to W20 for workshopping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-13-2023, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:49:20-07:00","id":1511522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511521#post1511521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly, Werewolf is nowhere near my main, so there could be information I'm not aware of, but a name change is actually something I would've wanted for this reason.<br /> <i>Fianna</i>, as far as I've ever been able to find out, is specifically Gaelic and has nothing to do with the Brythonic Celts. It feels like another case of Americans deciding Celtic=Irish, then remembering Scotland as an afterthought. If you're lucky, they know that Wales is not actually interchangeable with England. Then Cornwall, Brittany and the Isle of Mann are met with &quot;???&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Fianna are the Celtic tribe, not just the Irish/Hibernian tribe, then they've got a name from a legend with zero connection to 4/6 (or 3/6, unsure about the Manx) of the Celtic cultures. I mean, as I said, maybe they do have other names tucked away in a tribe book I've never read, in which case I rescind my complaints. But while &quot;Hart Warden&quot; doesn't really tie into any of the other myths that I'm aware of, I'd rather have Welsh werewolves call themselves something like <i>yr Ceidwad yr Hydd</i> than <i>Fianna/F\u00e8inne</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not happy with just slapping on a bland, meaningless name, but it'd do until I hunt down something Fianna-Cyclr-equivalent in the Mabinogion, or something.<br /> <br /> This is something of a moot point, because W5 has nothing to do with any of that, but at the very least I'm considering stealing the reboot name back to W20 for workshopping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> pretty much yeah, fianna is a legendary Scottish/irish warrior tradition similar to galloglasses. As Welsh primary it doesn't mean much to me outside of pan celtic pride....like a cousin who does well for himself.<br /> <br /> Hart wardens doesn't mean anything uniquely celtic to me the Irish people I know don't seem think much of it either. Pretty much every culture has sacred places and stories even the hated English and yanks (my tongue is in cheek).<br /> <br /> My idea for a Welsh is to refer to gellert and the wolf. Maybe gellert was a fianna lupus and the wolf was a spiral or something. Something like hounds of gellert? Maybe make them anti silver fang by saying prince llewellyn was their kinfolk. that I'd probably say irish/irish american are the most prominent camp in tribe so fianna works in that context.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-13-2023, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:54:24-07:00","id":1511523,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Knightingale;n1511520]<br /> <br /> What I meant is how the Hart Wardens description throws in the bit of them loving to be storytellers with the caveat that they also like to tell tall tales.[ /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah but every other society and culture ever does that isn't really a unique celtic trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-13-2023, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:58:45-07:00","id":1511524,"title":"","content":"I'm totally not planning to play a <s>Fianna</s> Hart Warden battle rapper if I'm ever not the one to be running the game, noooooooooo.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'm not, but that's only because I'll never be able to come up with rhymes on the spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:03:27-07:00","id":1511525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511522#post1511522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hart wardens doesn't mean anything uniquely celtic to me the Irish people I know don't seem think much of it either. Pretty much every culture has sacred places and stories even the hated English and yanks (my tongue is in cheek).<br /> <br /> My idea for a Welsh is to refer to gellert and the wolf. Maybe gellert was a fianna lupus and the wolf was a spiral or something.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>(...Wait, speaking of the English, is W5 changing the Get's name too, or are they still historically tied to Norse and Germanic peoples?)<br /> <br /> Gellert crossed my mind in the same way, as did drawing on the C\u0175n Annwn and having the criminals they hunt be formori. Though those hounds seem a bit grim for the cheery attitude the Fianna seem to be known for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:06:59-07:00","id":1511526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511523#post1511523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but every other society and culture ever does that isn't really a unique celtic trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about it being a uniquely Celtic trait, it's about it being part of the Fianna characterization in pre-W5 books. The old Fianna (and current Hart Warden) Tribal glyph is supposed to reference their traditions as storytellers by evoking sitting around a campfire telling stories in the night (like, it's basically &quot;fire, song/howl, moon&quot; by the Silver Record symbol guide). It's a hold over from the caricatures of Celtic (and really Irish) cultures that the Fianna wear originally based on; that they got rid of the name, but not the stereotyping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:25:27-07:00","id":1511527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511526#post1511526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about it being a uniquely Celtic trait, it's about it being part of the Fianna characterization in pre-W5 books. The old Fianna (and current Hart Warden) Tribal glyph is supposed to reference their traditions as storytellers by evoking sitting around a campfire telling stories in the night (like, it's basically &quot;fire, song/howl, moon&quot; by the Silver Record symbol guide). It's a hold over from the caricatures of Celtic (and really Irish) cultures that the Fianna wear originally based on; that they got rid of the name, but not the stereotyping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider that adequate to retain any sense of stereotype largely because I don't genrally consider the Hart wardens fianna and I especially don't consider them celts. They might fulfil the same role in tribe dynamics (maybe) but since they're not celts/irish it's meaningless. At that stage it's hard to even make the link much less care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-13-2023, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:38:51-07:00","id":1511528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511527#post1511527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't consider that adequate to retain any sense of stereotype largely because I don't genrally consider the Hart wardens fianna and I especially don't consider them celts. They might fulfil the same role in tribe dynamics (maybe) but since they're not celts/irish it's meaningless. At that stage it's hard to even make the link much less care.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, it took community-pushback to change the name. Until a couple weeks ago, the idea still had been to call them Fianna. As far as the developers were concerned, they were completely fine with the idea of calling them Fianna. And you might not care about obliquely referencing Irish sterotypes and the old Fianna-Tribe in this case but one it shows a lack of thoroughness in severing the link between human culture and the Tribes and two there's the potential of this leading to problems by doing the same thing with the Native American Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:39:33-07:00","id":1511529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511525#post1511525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...Wait, speaking of the English, is W5 changing the Get's name too, or are they still historically tied to Norse and Germanic peoples?)<br /> <br /> Gellert crossed my mind in the same way, as did drawing on the C\u0175n Annwn and having the criminals they hunt be formori. Though those hounds seem a bit grim for the cheery attitude the Fianna seem to be known for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd make sense for the Welsh fianna who are mentioned as being quite dour in Revised. I also think I'd have them being pressured by the silver fangs and glass walkers in South Wales and their strong points being elsewhere in the country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T02:50:53-07:00","id":1511530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511528#post1511528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, it took community-pushback to change the name. Until a couple weeks ago, the idea still had been to call them Fianna. As far as the developers were concerned, they were completely fine with the idea of calling them Fianna. And you might not care about obliquely referencing Irish sterotypes and the old Fianna-Tribe in this case but one it shows a lack of thoroughness in severing the link between human culture and the Tribes and two there's the potential of this leading to problems by doing the same thing with the Native American Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know and I hated it. Its the logical conclusion of how bland and a sterile w5 is going to be and how the sections of the community had a proactive role in the process. <br /> <br /> Don't cares a strong word since those links only really exist in the vaguest terms-at that stage getting mad requires a proactive desire to do so. The ghost council being the wizard tribe isn't enough for to get mad about because the ghost council arnt the uktena.<br /> <br /> if your soarce of irritation is the Tribe had a strong culture of storytelling like Irish people then it's effectively impossible to purge the Tribe of irish traits because your criteria is now so vague anything would qualify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T03:09:01-07:00","id":1511531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511530#post1511530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I know and I hated it. Its the logical conclusion of how bland and a sterile w5 is going to be and how the sections of the community had a proactive role in the process.<br /> <br /> Don't cares a strong word since those links only really exist in the vaguest terms-at that stage getting mad requires a proactive desire to do so. The ghost council being the wizard tribe isn't enough for to get mad about because the ghost council arnt the uktena.<br /> <br /> if your soarce of irritation is the Tribe had a strong culture of storytelling like Irish people then it's effectively impossible to purge the Tribe of irish traits because your criteria is now so vague anything would qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the &quot;They love to tell tall tales&quot; goes a bit further towards bringing up stereotypes here than just talking about a love for storytelling in general. And the criterium isn't vague at all, the criterium here is the old Fianna-Tribe. That's the link I'm specifically referencing here. And that the name-change had to happen through community-pushback is another sign of how this process of severing ties to human culture and ethnicity hasn't been very carefully executed. Which then also leads to moments like the picture of the GW-preview. It just doesn't feel like the care is put into this that is required here.<br /> <br /> And in the same manner the Ban of the Galestalker-Tribe of having to partake in a fresh kill daily certainly has a different ring to it when it's in the context of the old Younger Brother Tribe and the mythological creature that Tribe was named after - even though the point was to get away from that.<br /> <br /> Also, the blandness isn't a result of removing those links to human culture/ethnicity. If you do that, then you naturally have to come up with something compelling to take its place. That these new Tribe-write-ups fall short in that regard has nothing to do with that decision, I would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T04:07:53-07:00","id":1511533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511525#post1511525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...Wait, speaking of the English, is W5 changing the Get's name too, or are they still historically tied to Norse and Germanic peoples?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Bad End version of this timeline, they will use the Fenrir's name to justify why they fell to Haglust. Since, y'know, THEY were the ones sticking to a specific race.<br /> <br /> I mean, I DEARLY hope not, but it might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T05:26:07-07:00","id":1511537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511531#post1511531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I think the &quot;They love to tell tall tales&quot; goes a bit further towards bringing up stereotypes here than just talking about a love for storytelling in general. And the criterium isn't vague at all, the criterium here is the old Fianna-Tribe. That's the link I'm specifically referencing here. And that the name-change had to happen through community-pushback is another sign of how this process of severing ties to human culture and ethnicity hasn't been very carefully executed. Which then also leads to moments like the picture of the GW-preview. It just doesn't feel like the care is put into this that is required here.<br /> <br /> In the same manner the Ban of the Galestalker-Tribe of having to partake in a fresh kill daily certainly has a different ring to it when it's in the context of the old Younger Brother Tribe and the mythological creature that Tribe was named after - even though the point was to get away from that.<br /> <br /> Also, the blandness isn't a result of removing those links to human culture/ethnicity. If you do that, then you naturally have to come up with something compelling to take its place. That these new Tribe-write-ups fall short in that regard has nothing to do with that decision, I would say.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ehhhh maybe? I've never heard that one. Typical stereotypes about Irish people in my experiance is affable and easy going (still bad) except Northern Ireland where jaded and violent is the (ugly) steriotype ive also heard people from cork are quirky from irish people themselves. You on the British Isles?<br /> <br /> It is really if your criteria is &quot;has any traits that could be associated with the fianna&quot; then that is very very vague. Especially with traits like, strong oral tradition, warrior tribe or 'likes poetry'.<br /> <br /> Ironically I agree it comes from pushback from the ,'community' (lol) it's just I percieve it as a negative dynamic were both parties are caught in a negative re enforcement loop.<br /> <br /> the glasswalker thing is a completly differant issue and built on raw laziness of copied Google searches. <br /> <br /> my knowledgue of first nation peoples isn't as hot as a brit I can't really contest this but I do stand by my take on the Hart wardens. <br /> <br /> I'd say it's inevitable and linked. Youve got a completly sterilised tribe and its still not good enough. the only way you could get away with it would be if the hart wardens where implicitly the opposite or at least so different from the fianna as no tangential link would be acceptable as seen by the fact were currently arguing if tall tales is enough. Plus that's just werewolf the forsaken again anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T12:12:04-07:00","id":1511558,"title":"","content":"Garou tribes, encouraged by their totems and by the writer's need to make though provoking points of contrast, tend towards an extreme, but their extremes are found in lesser extents if not mirrored by the other tribes. The Fianna are obsessed with their image, the Get are elitist, the silver fangs are snobs.. but every tribe is to some extent, except in cases where the opposite is presented as some kind of extreme, like with Bone Gnawers. Every tribe had points to praise and points to reject, except the Croatan, because they're dead. <br /> <br /> Every single tribe made a statement. <br /> The Heart Wardens and new glass walkers don't. They say nothing. They are as aggressively mid as they could possibly be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T13:16:58-07:00","id":1511560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511526#post1511526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about it being a uniquely Celtic trait, it's about it being part of the Fianna characterization in pre-W5 books. The old Fianna (and current Hart Warden) Tribal glyph is supposed to reference their traditions as storytellers by evoking sitting around a campfire telling stories in the night (like, it's basically &quot;fire, song/howl, moon&quot; by the Silver Record symbol guide). It's a hold over from the caricatures of Celtic (and really Irish) cultures that the Fianna wear originally based on; that they got rid of the name, but not the stereotyping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not like they have kept a stereotype: Fianna fulfilled a thematic role which was stereotyped into Irishness, along with a sizeable chunk of other much more unhealty stereotypes. <br /> <br /> Hart Wardens nurture Gaian holy places and the legends they are associated with: they are sacred storytellers, figures which are fairly universal in traditional cultures. <br /> <br /> The concept remains, now applicable to characters from all over the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T13:26:05-07:00","id":1511561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511537#post1511537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ironically I agree it comes from pushback from the ,'community' (lol) it's just I percieve it as a negative dynamic were both parties are caught in a negative re enforcement loop.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We are definitely in an unfortunate dynamic of this kind: every possible anticipation about W5 is usually evaluated as absolutistic and in connection with former lore, metaplot and presentation.<br /> <br /> So, if we are told Garou have troubles living between two worlds of Men and Spirits, we immediately jump to the conclusion that they are hated by spirits and by humans, and if we don't see this kind of extreme situation we think the presentation is incoherent.<br /> <br /> Or if we, are told Garou are mostly Homids, this must mean Lupus is gone or actively discouraged, or Fera must be chopped.<br /> <br /> Or, if tribes are universal, they are either still too much the old tribe and not universal enough, or too far from the past lore.<br /> <br /> I fear that, so far, the discussion is so dominated by heated feelings that it's just going to end up as a mammuth exercise in finding every possible problem it may be singled out in the new game.<br /> <br /> That was probably bound to happen, but still it's a pity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-13-2023, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T14:59:18-07:00","id":1511567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511560#post1511560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not like they have kept a stereotype: Fianna fulfilled a thematic role which was stereotyped into Irishness, along with a sizeable chunk of other much more unhealty stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Hart Wardens nurture Gaian holy places and the legends they are associated with: they are sacred storytellers, figures which are fairly universal in traditional cultures.<br /> <br /> The concept remains, now applicable to characters from all over the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, as Knightinggale pointed out, they did keep the stereotyping even if they're trying to make it more universal. The problem is that the &quot;sacred storytellers&quot; has nothing to do with the Hart Wardens except for the fact that they're formerly the Fianna. None of the Hart Warden verbs have anything to do with being sacred storytellers. Their verbs make them out to be more muses and historians than performers as they <i>nurture</i> and <i>cultivate </i>art/history they care about. The stuff about their gatherings turning into recitations of stories and tall tales, makes no sense as being there except we know that the Hart Wardens are based on the storytelling happy Fianna of the older versions of the game.<br /> <br /> There's no case made in the preview for why the protectors and nurtures of sacred places are also the sacred storytellers (or, when you have 11 Tribes, you'd want to combine those distinct concepts into one of them). It only makes sense because they're retaining stuff from the Fianna, and their storytelling tradition is part of the caricature of the American based perceptions of Irish people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511561#post1511561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are definitely in an unfortunate dynamic of this kind: every possible anticipation about W5 is usually evaluated as absolutistic and in connection with former lore, metaplot and presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why shouldn't the 5th edition of a game be evaluated in comparison to the previous four editions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if we are told Garou have troubles living between two worlds of Men and Spirits, we immediately jump to the conclusion that they are hated by spirits and by humans, and if we don't see this kind of extreme situation we think the presentation is incoherent.<br /> <br /> Or if we, are told Garou are mostly Homids, this must mean Lupus is gone or actively discouraged, or Fera must be chopped.<br /> <br /> Or, if tribes are universal, they are either still too much the old tribe and not universal enough, or too far from the past lore. </div> </div> </div>You are giving a gigantic pass to Paradox here. They put out a bunch of preview material, and did a bunch of Q&amp;As and videos about W5. They have set expectations, and people are reacting to that. It's not our fault if Paradox says X in one place, and then says Y in another place, and we complain about that inconsistency. If they said X in both places you would have a much stronger point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fear that, so far, the discussion is so dominated by heated feelings that it's just going to end up as a mammuth exercise in finding every possible problem it may be singled out in the new game. </div> </div> </div>Do you think you're making the situation better or worse? You're part of the community and part of the discussion too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was probably bound to happen, but still it's a pity. </div> </div> </div>Paradox didn't have to go the whole, &quot;we're rebooting the game, but only kinda sorta,&quot; route. It's a bad kind of compromise that yes, makes it inevitable that there's heated debate about the game because selling people on how the whole pick-and-choose method of what to keep, what to adjust, and what to toss out completely is hard work that Paradox hasn't actually done yet. Maybe they're confident the book will do that on its own, but that's hard to imagine given how things went with V5 and H5.<br /> <br /> They have also, whether intentional or not, communicated a lot that W5 is basically going to be a rushed project. In a matter of months it went from, &quot;we're starting previews, but bare with us if we can't answer certain things because major parts of the game are still in development,&quot; to, &quot;it's ready to ship to the printers even if thankfully it hasn't yet so we had time to fix that art snafu.&quot; I might not agree that W5 is communicating a sense of not caring, but it's certainly setting itself up to be full of errors regardless. Those errors are going to fuel negative critical analysis of the game.<br /> <br /> Maybe Paradox is too used to being a video game company and being able to patch games or something, but that doesn't explain why Renegade isn't pushing back on getting out W5 for Gencon successfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T16:17:31-07:00","id":1511571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511537#post1511537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is really if your criteria is &quot;has any traits that could be associated with the fianna&quot; then that is very very vague. Especially with traits like, strong oral tradition, warrior tribe or 'likes poetry'.<br /> <br /> Ironically I agree it comes from pushback from the ,'community' (lol) it's just I percieve it as a negative dynamic were both parties are caught in a negative re enforcement loop.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's inevitable and linked. Youve got a completly sterilised tribe and its still not good enough. <b>the only way you could get away with it would be if the hart wardens where implicitly the opposite or at least so different from the fianna as no tangential link would be acceptable as seen by the fact were currently arguing if tall tales is enough.</b> Plus that's just werewolf the forsaken again anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I emphasized there is what needs to be done. I know, it's a lot of hoops to jump through to accommodate this but the issue here is: This is what the developers wanted! The only reason we're talking about Hart Wardens and &quot;How much of old-Fianna-DNA is in there...?&quot; is because the essential W5-setup is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; - or in other words &quot;It isn't the WtA you used to know but is not <i>not </i>WtA.&quot;. Constantly W5 asks us to think of WtA but then also to remind us what's different. It isn't even a reboot. After all, Gaia's dead/dying, the setting's mid-Apocalpyse, the Garou-Nation has fallen and the Tribes have been changed in various degrees... This is all new stuff for WtA. The developers stated that there are no longer any links between human culture/ethnicity and the Tribes have been rewritten, sometimes even renamed, to accommodate that new paradigm. And so that's how the Tribes are to be evaluated. It's the developers who set up the criteria here. They say this is what they want to do and they will be criticized based on how well they do it.<br /> <br /> Of course, something like WtF is a much better approach from a worldbuilding-perspective since if you don't wanna do WtA, just swiping the slate clean and restart from 0 (and only take WtA as a distant inspiration) is a much better approach to doing something new. Having to jump through all these hoops of both being a new and different WtA while still having to make sure it's still somehow WtA in the end seems like a needless hassle to me. But the developers are going down that path, so... it is what it is, I guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T00:33:33-07:00","id":1511586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511571#post1511571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I emphasized there is what needs to be done. I know, it's a lot of hoops to jump through to accommodate this but the issue here is: This is what the developers wanted! The only reason we're talking about Hart Wardens and &quot;How much of old-Fianna-DNA is in there...?&quot; is because the essential W5-setup is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; - or in other words &quot;It isn't the WtA you used to know but is not <i>not </i>WtA.&quot;. Constantly W5 asks us to think of WtA but then also to remind us what's different. It isn't even a reboot. After all, Gaia's dead/dying, the setting's mid-Apocalpyse, the Garou-Nation has fallen and the Tribes have been changed in various degrees... This is all new stuff for WtA. The developers stated that there are no longer any links between human culture/ethnicity and the Tribes have been rewritten, sometimes even renamed, to accommodate that new paradigm. And so that's how the Tribes are to be evaluated. It's the developers who set up the criteria here. They say this is what they want to do and they will be criticized based on how well they do it.<br /> <br /> Of course, something like WtF is a much better approach from a worldbuilding-perspective since if you don't wanna do WtA, just swiping the slate clean and restart from 0 (and only take WtA as a distant inspiration) is a much better approach to doing something new. Having to jump through all these hoops of both being a new and different WtA while still having to make sure it's still somehow WtA in the end seems like a needless hassle to me. But the developers are going down that path, so... it is what it is, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I think that's our point of deviation. Because that's just werewolf the forsaken again (if a bit more 1st ed requiem vs masquare really) so sounds boring and pointless.<br /> <br /> I don't think what you're proposing can be done in a way where its 'good' it's just going to be compared to forsaken which if anything is going to be even less flattering than classic apocalypse. It says a lot that the current two tribe write ups are somehow duller than the blood talons in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't think the Hart wardens have enough dna in them to be considered fianna and I certainly don't consider them celts. As you commented by your standards of success the hearth wardens would have to be consciously alien from the fianna with such strict criteria which then leads to other issues.<br /> <br /> On reflection this whole reboot seems like a bad idea full stop but then again reboots usually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-14-2023, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T09:04:07-07:00","id":1511618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511533#post1511533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Bad End version of this timeline, they will use the Fenrir's name to justify why they fell to Haglust. Since, y'know, THEY were the ones sticking to a specific race.<br /> <br /> I mean, I DEARLY hope not, but it might.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think it\u2019ll be that. I really don\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T09:15:00-07:00","id":1511619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511586#post1511586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I think that's our point of deviation. Because that's just werewolf the forsaken again (if a bit more 1st ed requiem vs masquare really) so sounds boring and pointless.<br /> <br /> I don't think what you're proposing can be done in a way where its 'good' it's just going to be compared to forsaken which if anything is going to be even less flattering than classic apocalypse. It says a lot that the current two tribe write ups are somehow duller than the blood talons in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't think the Hart wardens have enough dna in them to be considered fianna and I certainly don't consider them celts. As you commented by your standards of success the hearth wardens would have to be consciously alien from the fianna with such strict criteria which then leads to other issues.<br /> <br /> On reflection this whole reboot seems like a bad idea full stop but then again reboots usually are.</div> </div> </div> </div>the heart wardens are a new tribe. The complaints initially for the 5th fianna was it looked different from legacy. Changing the name really just cements that it\u2019s a different tribe. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll push back on the forsaken thing. We aren\u2019t getting forsaken 3. My forsaken tribes aren\u2019t coming back. The world isn\u2019t coming back. The content is clearly apocalypse. They\u2019re just broadening the tribes because it\u2019s the best way to modernize and avoid offending people at this point. That\u2019s really what it boils down to. What\u2019s not offensive. <br /> <br /> that\u2019s not to say it won\u2019t be good. I think it will be. It\u2019s just the reality. <br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, making the fenrir fall instead of hyper modernizing them makes them even more hard ass and I\u2019m here for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:38:11-07:00","id":1511633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511619#post1511619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the heart wardens are a new tribe. The complaints initially for the 5th fianna was it looked different from legacy. Changing the name really just cements that it\u2019s a different tribe.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll push back on the forsaken thing. We aren\u2019t getting forsaken 3. My forsaken tribes aren\u2019t coming back. The world isn\u2019t coming back. The content is clearly apocalypse. They\u2019re just broadening the tribes because it\u2019s the best way to modernize and avoid offending people at this point. That\u2019s really what it boils down to. What\u2019s not offensive.<br /> <br /> that\u2019s not to say it won\u2019t be good. I think it will be. It\u2019s just the reality.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, making the fenrir fall instead of hyper modernizing them makes them even more hard ass and I\u2019m here for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The content is not Apocalypse, because it's some bizarre game with a fixation on &quot;street level&quot; stuff even though Apocalypse wasn't about that at its core. If it were Apocalypse, the tribe writeups would focus on their preferred targets in a war, just as Forsaken 2nd edition tribe writeups were focused on their preferences for the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T12:33:25-07:00","id":1511641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511633#post1511633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The content is not Apocalypse, because it's some bizarre game with a fixation on &quot;street level&quot; stuff even though Apocalypse wasn't about that at its core. If it were Apocalypse, the tribe writeups would focus on their preferred targets in a war, just as Forsaken 2nd edition tribe writeups were focused on their preferences for the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was told a lot times - W5 Garou aren't warriors, they are survaivers who already lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T13:23:29-07:00","id":1511645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511633#post1511633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The content is not Apocalypse, because it's some bizarre game with a fixation on &quot;street level&quot; stuff even though Apocalypse wasn't about that at its core. If it were Apocalypse, the tribe writeups would focus on their preferred targets in a war, just as Forsaken 2nd edition tribe writeups were focused on their preferences for the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I\u2019ve read of the preview is reminding me a lot of early first edition apocalypse. Which was a lot more focused on the first change experience. 2nd and revised did the big world ending meta plot stuff a lot more, with w20 really just reinforcing it in a big way. <br /> <br /> none of this reads to me like forsaken, which I\u2019m a big fan of. It\u2019s a distinctly different tone, aside the vagueness of the tribes, but even forsaken tribes aren\u2019t vague. More honed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T13:26:34-07:00","id":1511646,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> to carry the lazy artist thing over here, why are none of the images crinos form? I would have hoped for homid, crinos, and lupus. Though maybe without the importance of breed they feel it doesn\u2019t matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T14:05:22-07:00","id":1511650,"title":"","content":"Um, so, I have a new question about this write up; <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Such are the nights when the Local Legend haunts the wilds, prowling for the flesh of the greedy...&quot; </div> </div> </div> etc, etc.<br /> <br /> that wording with &quot;prowling for flesh&quot; kind of implies predation to me. Soooo have the youth decided the Litany is optional or is eating people a thing the Garou are allowed to do now? <br /> <br /> <br /> <s>Also thinking on it, using the white furred underworld canids associated with death and the spirits of the dead as the basis for Welsh werewolves would actually directly connect to the other, white furred death/underworld-associated (Brythonic) Celtic tribe, but that's not really relevant to W5 or the preview, so I'll just let the topic stop there having gotten it out of my system while I go take a hammer to WtA canon.</s><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T14:15:11-07:00","id":1511651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511619#post1511619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the heart wardens are a new tribe. The complaints initially for the 5th fianna was it looked different from legacy. Changing the name really just cements that it\u2019s a different tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... kinda the exact opposite of what happened.<br /> <br /> Paradox's previews said that in W5 the Tribes would be divorced from specific cultures and instead be global phenomena largely empowered by individual compatibility with Patron spirits. This justified the name change of Older and Younger Brother, since their old names only made sense as strictly pre-European colonization American Tribes.<br /> <br /> Fans then pointed out that the Fianna still had a name that too similar to legacy: Fianna only makes sense as a name if the Tribe's origins are kept tied to a specific culture. The complaints that the Fianna were to similar to legacy, not too different.<br /> <br /> The name wasn't changed to solidify that the Hart Wardens are actually meant to be different in base concept from the Fianna, but to satisfy the fan dislike of the inconsistently applied logic of why the names were changed. There's no evidence that they changed anything about the Hart Wardens besides the name (esp. with how late in the process that change occurred).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:08:11-07:00","id":1511656,"title":"","content":"And the one Tribe that's become bad guys seems to still be called &quot;the Get of Fenris&quot;, which means we have ~10 tribes without a clear cultural link to a human culture, and a group of monstrous extremists who are directly tied to Scandinavian cultures. I'm sure this will be a big hit with Norse fans!<br /> <br /> (thankfully Viking-style paganism isn't very popular with nerds at all /j)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:39:15-07:00","id":1511662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511650#post1511650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, so, I have a new question about this write up;<br /> etc, etc.<br /> <br /> that wording with &quot;prowling for flesh&quot; kind of implies predation to me. Soooo have the youth decided the Litany is optional or is eating people a thing the Garou are allowed to do now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>From what has been revealed, yes. Litany is now considered hidebound and flawed.<br /> <br /> From the preview:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Litany, the:</b> A set of maxims and mores by which werewolf society conducted itself in the past, but viewed askance in a modern context as insufficient to help the Garou prevent the Apocalypse\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> So, unless that was just the writer being fancy, long pig is on the menu XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:58:45-07:00","id":1511667,"title":"","content":"Caught up with the news and the thread!<br /> <br /> 1. Someone proposed \u201cWild (Wyld?) Hunt\u201d as the new/not-Fianna some time ago somewhere, and man I wish that was official instead.<br /> <br /> 2. Did the folks who keep referring to the W5 stuff as Forsaken-like, like, decided to completely ignore Forsaken 2e or something\u2026? I mean, the similarities are there yes, can\u2019t deny that, but I still can\u2019t see why it\u2019s similar enough to be used as a label.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T16:02:49-07:00","id":1511668,"title":"","content":"It's a weird example of crossed wires to both remove the potentially offensive parts of the Litany *and* say it's no longer widely observed in the same update/reimagining/reboot.<br /> <br /> If it's bigoted and old fashioned, then go with that. If it's sanitized and safe, go with that. Why are you doing this weird flip flopping where you've both sanitized *and* exiled it.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth I do have an issue with W20's litany, but less with the book or its text, and more with the fan response; weirdly there seem to be people who drink the IC koolaid and believe that the rules are all genuinely good, when they're clearly intended to be a mixture of sensible/obvious (don't betray your Caern, don't eat human flesh), iffy (ruler can never be challenged in war time, the highest in station always get the first rewards) and outright foul (promoting mandatory euthanasia, discouraging caring for the sick/disabled/elderly, forbidding a category of romantic relationships). The Litany is meant to be a reflection of the Garou as a whole. You can see a noble goal in there, and good practical steps being taken in the most obvious ways towards fulfilling that goal, but clearly not optimized for the modern age. You can also see three (or more) Tribes rejecting some parts of the Litany entirely and proposing alternative tenets. It's complicated and interesting!<br /> <br /> Kind of thing you could run a game on... or get rid of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T16:03:36-07:00","id":1511669,"title":"","content":"Wyld Hunt is indeed a much better Fianna-esque name, if you wanna remove the Irish word! Hell I'm surprised there isn't a Camp of that name!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T16:09:11-07:00","id":1511671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511656#post1511656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the one Tribe that's become bad guys seems to still be called &quot;the Get of Fenris&quot;, which means we have ~10 tribes without a clear cultural link to a human culture, and a group of monstrous extremists who are directly tied to Scandinavian cultures. I'm sure this will be a big hit with Norse fans!<br /> <br /> (thankfully Viking-style paganism isn't very popular with nerds at all /j)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get of Fenris always said humans worshiping the Norse gods were doing it wrong. But now I guess they're the ones who are wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T16:13:36-07:00","id":1511672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511667#post1511667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Did the folks who keep referring to the W5 stuff as Forsaken-like, like, decided to completely ignore Forsaken 2e or something\u2026? I mean, the similarities are there yes, can\u2019t deny that, but I still can\u2019t see why it\u2019s similar enough to be used as a label.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it isn't Forsaken 2nd ed that I'm comparing it to. Forsaken 1st ed had a lot of growing pains to do to stand on its own and W5 seems to copy the worst of them.<br /> <br /> In all fairness, making comparisons now that we are getting previews is meaningless. Because Forsaken 1st ed STILL was focused on the characters being werewolves. W5 is more and more focusing not on the horror of being a garou OR the horror of the Wyrm's effects. The focus is on humanity and the horror seems to be how hidebound the old Nation was. We have gotten few previews so far BUT all of them have repeated this same mentality (aside from that one sidebar); The character you play is defined by their civilian life more than their supernatural one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T20:28:57-07:00","id":1511689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511672#post1511672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but it isn't Forsaken 2nd ed that I'm comparing it to. Forsaken 1st ed had a lot of growing pains to do to stand on its own and W5 seems to copy the worst of them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, I must\u2019ve put myself in some cognitive trap then. Gonna have to jump out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> In all fairness, making comparisons now that we are getting previews is meaningless. Because Forsaken 1st ed STILL was focused on the characters being werewolves. W5 is more and more focusing not on the horror of being a garou OR the horror of the Wyrm's effects. The focus is on humanity and the horror seems to be how hidebound the old Nation was. We have gotten few previews so far BUT all of them have repeated this same mentality (aside from that one sidebar); The character you play is defined by their civilian life more than their supernatural one.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it\u2019s strange\u2026 I mean, for all the flak Forsaken 1e gets for being bland and too local-focused, it still had the Brethren Wars and the Maeljin looming over them as a Big threat. Shame that that part is, of all things they can take notes from Forsaken, largely shrugged over\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T22:00:15-07:00","id":1511693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511689#post1511689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmm, I must\u2019ve put myself in some cognitive trap then. Gonna have to jump out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, it\u2019s strange\u2026 I mean, for all the flak Forsaken 1e gets for being bland and too local-focused, it still had the Brethren Wars and the Maeljin looming over them as a Big threat. Shame that that part is, of all things they can take notes from Forsaken, largely shrugged over\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> forsaken (and awakening) are interesting in the core books are quite bland and have that 'street' obsession but later books expand and flesh out quickly and efficiently. The lunar tribes might be dangerously close to just being another auspice in the corebook but lodges are full of neat ideas.<br /> <br /> the issue with w5 is linked with v5s disinterest in expanding the setting or introducing meaningful conflicts. 5th has aggressively removing things removing stuff from the game wereas nwod was keen to bring stuff in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-15-2023, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T01:33:29-07:00","id":1511701,"title":"","content":"That idea of W5 being about this new generation of Garou still doesn't quite make sense to me. They think the Garou-Nation was a backwards-looking organization (that is now already gone anyway), they don't like the Litany, they think the Garou Elders are losers and in general, think Garou traditions are too old-fashioned... Why would these werewolves even wanna call themselves Garou...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T02:02:52-07:00","id":1511702,"title":"","content":"Honestly, why are we even keeping the nation if we're tossing out its history (good and bad) and saying that it's irrelevant. If this is a reimagining, why not make new bespoke social structures instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T02:43:23-07:00","id":1511703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511702#post1511702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, why are we even keeping the nation if we're tossing out its history (good and bad) and saying that it's irrelevant. If this is a reimagining, why not make new bespoke social structures instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the same reason V5 has the Camarilla even though the Anarchs are the preferred faction; There needs to be the Old Guard for the PCs to rebel at.<br /> <br /> How can the PCs show they are SO much more Enlightened and Modern if there is no contrast? /s<br /> <br /> If I am being honest, do we even need the BSDs in W5? We already have the Elders, the Fenrir, Second Inquisition and other packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T02:55:13-07:00","id":1511704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511701#post1511701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That idea of W5 being about this new generation of Garou still doesn't quite make sense to me. They think the Garou-Nation was a backwards-looking organization (that is now already gone anyway), they don't like the Litany, they think the Garou Elders are losers and in general, think Garou traditions are too old-fashioned... Why would these werewolves even wanna call themselves Garou...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it can make sense if you consider that the Garou-Nation, the Elders, the Litany all failed and allowed Gaia to die. So in that regard, none of those people or ideas worked or were successful. That's the premise for W5 and it's potentially interesting. At the same time though, I haven't seen any ideas as what new direction the new Garou are going to be going and what they'll be doing differently from what the old Garou did? So far, it seems like it's mostly just complaining and hanging around the Caern or basically doing mostly the same stuff you would have been doing in earlier Werewolf editions. Thats... not interesting and it seems like W5 is going to have a difficult time living up the premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T03:08:45-07:00","id":1511706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511704#post1511704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it can make sense if you consider that the Garou-Nation, the Elders, the Litany all failed and allowed Gaia to die. So in that regard, none of those people or ideas worked or were successful. That's the premise for W5 and it's potentially interesting. At the same time though, I haven't seen any ideas as what new direction the new Garou are going to be going and what they'll be doing differently from what the old Garou did? So far, it seems like it's mostly just complaining and hanging around the Caern or basically doing mostly the same stuff you would have been doing in earlier Werewolf editions. Thats... not interesting and it seems like W5 is going to have a difficult time living up the premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. Nothing wrong with going in that direction. All these things are flawed, there's no reason to cling to them anymore, especially since the setting's mid-Apocalypse but... now what? With VtM the Camarilla can be rejected/fought against and you can point at the Anarchs as the alternative. With W5, though, there's no alternative presented to being a Garou so rejecting the idea of Garou and their traditions to such a huge degree just leaves the whole thing adrift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T04:17:51-07:00","id":1511708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511706#post1511706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Completely agree. Nothing wrong with going in that direction. All these things are flawed, there's no reason to cling to them anymore, especially since the setting's mid-Apocalypse but... now what? With VtM the Camarilla can be rejected/fought against and you can point at the Anarchs as the alternative. With W5, though, there's no alternative presented to being a Garou so rejecting the idea of Garou and their traditions to such a huge degree just leaves the whole thing adrift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the thing though over time the Anarchs invariably just become the Camarilla again, will the Next Gen Garou just become the Nation again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T04:54:56-07:00","id":1511711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511708#post1511708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats the thing though over time the Anarchs invariably just become the Camarilla again, will the Next Gen Garou just become the Nation again?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Vampire has a system for non-allied vampires. Werewolf tried it but very quickly realised the focus was best on the Nation vs the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> And in the end, VtM is mostly about sects fighting with each other. There is freedom in that that WtA never had. But W5 is trying to use the same method that VtM had, when the threat in WtA has never been as much internal as external.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:24:34-07:00","id":1511715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511711#post1511711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that Vampire has a system for non-allied vampires. Werewolf tried it but very quickly realised the focus was best on the Nation vs the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> And in the end, VtM is mostly about sects fighting with each other. There is freedom in that that WtA never had. But W5 is trying to use the same method that VtM had, when the threat in WtA has never been as much internal as external.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think the Garou-society works better when player-characters have to navigate it despite how flawed and dysfunctional it is. It's an obstacle and tension-point for the game but it's mostly just something that occasionally interrupts the main-thing: The War against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> And on the other hand, investing in the idea of &quot;What would a good Garou-Nation look like?&quot; and having player-characters pursue that feels like it would distract too much from the Wyrm as the main-antagonist. Suddenly the main-antagonist are the factions within Garou-society who are debating over what the new Garou-Nation should be like.<br /> <br /> But the W5-status-quo starts with no tension at all when it comes to Garou-society, doesn't it? After all, it simply blew up the whole thing before any player-characters got involved. Besides, how much will anyone really care if the game's perspective is &quot;It's gone and it was bad anyway.&quot;? Why would any new want to engage with this part of the game when that's the take the corebook is giving them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:37:03-07:00","id":1511716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511715#post1511715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the W5-status-quo starts with no tension at all when it comes to Garou-society, doesn't it? After all, it simply blew up the whole thing before any player-characters got involved. Besides, how much will anyone really care if the game's perspective is &quot;It's gone and it was bad anyway.&quot;? Why would any new want to engage with this part of the game when that's the take the corebook is giving them...</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems there SHOULD be tension, given how many times the previews focus on the old ways vs new ones. As stated before in this thread, there isn't really any sense of urgency about the Apocalypse. If anything, it seems like a GOOD thing as now young garou can fulfil their dreams of being baristas and not bother with the war.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:46:28-07:00","id":1511717,"title":"","content":"The litany and many Garou customs are terrible from a normal, well adjusted human perspective but for Garou who are structurally between a military and a cult (marines?) most of them make a great deal of sense even in the modern era, the only real modern problems being -kill the elderly- and perhaps -greatest of station- <br /> <br /> Garou society is really complex with so many rites and howls and traditions and... You're meant to transport yourselves into another world, even if that world is earth. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like a flawed nation. <br /> <i>Yeah the wars of rage were probably a mistake but those bastet are too few to protect that big juicy caern so we should push them out... <br /> <br /> this silver fang family are terrible rulers but they're great at klaive duels and using the laws to their advantage. <br /> <br /> These two bloodlines have a big multi-generational feud and while they'd never sink to open warfare due to other parties it's very clear that their rivalry often gets in the way of duty</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:48:34-07:00","id":1511718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511706#post1511706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Completely agree. Nothing wrong with going in that direction. All these things are flawed, there's no reason to cling to them anymore, especially since the setting's mid-Apocalypse but... now what? With VtM the Camarilla can be rejected/fought against and you can point at the Anarchs as the alternative. With W5, though, there's no alternative presented to being a Garou so rejecting the idea of Garou and their traditions to such a huge degree just leaves the whole thing adrift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the big issue with the anarchs is they don't really have any ideas going forward or its just a kratocracy. It's actually a bit of a problem in v5 that the anarchs are a complete joke when you start to look at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:58:07-07:00","id":1511720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511645#post1511645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I\u2019ve read of the preview is reminding me a lot of early first edition apocalypse. Which was a lot more focused on the first change experience. 2nd and revised did the big world ending meta plot stuff a lot more, with w20 really just reinforcing it in a big way.<br /> <br /> none of this reads to me like forsaken, which I\u2019m a big fan of. It\u2019s a distinctly different tone, aside the vagueness of the tribes, but even forsaken tribes aren\u2019t vague. More honed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't know where you get that from, when the First Change doesn't seem to be talked about at all? Especially not for the tribe writeups of example Garou. Also, 2e and Revised didn't completely blow the entire background setting up for W:tA. Metaplot for Werewolf was always very light-handed compared to Vampire and Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T06:09:46-07:00","id":1511721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511717#post1511717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The litany and many Garou customs are terrible from a normal, well adjusted human perspective but for Garou who are structurally between a military and a cult (marines?) most of them make a great deal of sense even in the modern era, the only real modern problems being -kill the elderly- and perhaps -greatest of station-</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is because I like to play Philodox, but for the most part I'd say the Litany is far from the worst set of laws in WoD. For one, there are MULTIPLE tenets focusing on peaceful resolution, there are the &quot;Be kind to those beneath you&quot; and &quot;Do not eat the flesh of humans&quot; laws and even the Leader Shall not be Challenged law has its twin in Leader SHALL be challenged during peacetime. As in, the law is to ensure that the pack/sept fights as one and solves its issues when they can.<br /> <br /> Garou are absolutely monsters, but the way the young garou reject the Litany in W5 sounds weird since most tenets are there to support co-operation or protect Gaia. The ones that aren't either don't matter anymore (Garou shall not mate with garou), are disliked for the chain of command or are nebulous like Tend thy Sickness one.<br /> <br /> And I mean, one of the laws IS forbidding cannibalism, so uh...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T11:52:56-07:00","id":1511731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511716#post1511716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems there SHOULD be tension, given how many times the previews focus on the old ways vs new ones. As stated before in this thread, there isn't really any sense of urgency about the Apocalypse. If anything, it seems like a GOOD thing as now young garou can fulfil their dreams of being baristas and not bother with the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think W5 will be about young vs. old. The way I picture this is the design of WOD5E follows this pattern:<ul><li>You take the barebones of the old WOD-splat-setting and create two buckets, one is called status-quo and the other is the main-antagonist.</li> <li>For the main-antagonist V5 has the Sabbat, H5 has their supernatural monsters/Quarries and W5 has the Wyrm. Those are irredeemably evil and not a player-option.</li> <li>Then you take all the elements in the setting with power and influence and they are put into the status-quo-bucket. With V5 it's the Camarilla, with H5 it's the hunter-orgs and with W5 it's the Garou-traditions, Garou-Elders and Garou-Nation.</li> <li>Next comes this idea: status-quo=bad and fighting against status-quo=good. So you get &quot;Camarilla=bad Anarchs=good&quot;, &quot;hunter-orgs=bad Hunters with Drive/Hunter-cells=good&quot; and &quot;Garou-traditions/Garou-Elders=bad Rejecting Garou-traditions/young Garou=good&quot;</li> <li>And you finish it by re-writing the setting to accommodate this. In V5 you get the Beckoning weakening the Camarilla and explaining the rise of the Anarchs that way. With H5 the corebook is very concerned with telling you how bad hunter-orgs are and so you get this setup where Governmental hunter-orgs are repressive and authoritarian, Religious hunter-orgs are all zealots and fanatics, Academic hunter-orgs are more interested in their research than saving human lives and Vigilantes are the &quot;If you <i>only </i>care about killing monsters, you're playing H5 wrong.&quot;-faction. In the case of W5 you get a mix of the two: Similar to the Beckoning the setting gets &quot;blown up&quot; allowing for the anti-status-quo-factions to have a seat at the table and you get the Get of Fenris as &quot;If you <i>only </i>care about fighting the Wyrm, you're playing W5 wrong.&quot;-faction.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T15:32:01-07:00","id":1511744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Half the time I read a &quot;Oh this is like Forsaken.&quot; comment somewhere I don't know what people even mean because it's so vague and at best pointing to some period in relative early 1e CofD that I can't help but feel it doesn't really hold up to scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not coming from nowhere.<br /> <br /> The war against the Wyrm was a setting problem that could be tackled in a variety of ways and at many different levels, and the general restructuring of the Garou nation and textual de-emphasis of the cosmic and global ways of handling that problem in favor of local and regional fronts is pretty openly reflective of the way Forsaken (and Chronicles on the whole) favored the understanding of the Uratha's duty as a more individual affair as opposed to a (more) tightly controlled effort. For all the stereotyping that was put into the Tribes, they were distinct from Forsaken's Tribes for their specificity in terms of the real world environments, cultures, and history, and the movement away from tying Tribes to those aspects in favor of broader appeal again looks more like the Uratha's situation. What we've got on Renown feels like it's trying to get into the utility of the trait as a main feature as opposed to how it was handled previously.*<br /> <br /> And of course, all of this is on the back of how Masquerade 5E and Reckoning 5E were handled, which also has a lot of Chronicles-esque decisions made for their setting, compacted with various creator's histories and appreciation of Chronicles material.<br /> <br /> If the changes don't particularly feel substantial, well, part of that is not having the whole picture in the form of the final book, but the bigger issue is that a lot of Apocalypse's surface text is still aligned with the feel of Apocalypse, but a lot of the structure, operation, and perspective of the war against the Wyrm has taken a turn in such a way as to feel more like how business is handled by the Uratha rather than the Garou-and that would be fine if it worked for the sensibilities of an ongoing franchise, but it feels very at odds with the way Apocalypse has operated before. Really, that's where it's most apparent-the way the flowery curtains don't match the military industrial complex, as it were.<br /> <br /> *and if it seems like I'm being vague, again, I'm a fan of World of Darkness games, but I wouldn't call myself the most versed in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T03:13:22-07:00","id":1511784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Half the time I read a &quot;Oh this is like Forsaken.&quot; comment somewhere I don't know what people even mean because it's so vague and at best pointing to some period in relative early 1e CofD that I can't help but feel it doesn't really hold up to scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many things W5 copies from WtF 1st edition. The limited war-form, tribes being tied to renown, the war form being unable to use weapons (even though they kept the weapon DESIGNED for that form), renown amount serving as a way to get gifts and so on.<br /> <br /> But you are right, this does not sound like Forsaken at all. Forsaken was about dealing with the Pure, hostile spirit would and so on. The focus is not on the daily lives of the uratha.<br /> <br /> W5's focus is on the mundane lives of the garou, the tribe previews focusing not on the fight against the Wyrm or the Apocalypse but on what jobs and daily duties the garou has.<br /> <br /> So the best way I can describe W5 as we know it now, is taking aspects of Forsaken and inserting them in and then focusing on mundanity over spiritualism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:15:42-07:00","id":1511788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511784#post1511784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many things W5 copies from WtF 1st edition. The limited war-form, tribes being tied to renown, the war form being unable to use weapons (even though they kept the weapon DESIGNED for that form), renown amount serving as a way to get gifts and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the Garou-Kin-dynamic which is eerily similar to how the First Change was described in 1E including the idea of Packs running around looking for would-be werewolves pre-First-Change and competing with each other over who gets to recruit them. And the bit of trying to trigger the First Change is also there. In the Glossary of the W5-preview it's called &quot;Kinseeking&quot; but re-reading the section in WtF 1E... if it's still the same as it was described last October, it's pretty much the same idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:20:23-07:00","id":1511790,"title":"","content":"That just sounds fucking stupid. I assume they dropped that from 2nd for a reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:24:48-07:00","id":1511791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Half the time I read a &quot;Oh this is like Forsaken.&quot; comment somewhere I don't know what people even mean because it's so vague and at best pointing to some period in relative early 1e CofD that I can't help but feel it doesn't really hold up to scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, a lot of early Forsaken material was designed in a way to demonstrate how its NOT WtA withouht establishing what it IS. The tonal discussions and disjunctions are very similar in the discussion of the games and thats where the similarity of the games stem from.<br /> <br /> WtF (with a ton of supplements) or WtF2 are games that built their own identity on their own merits. You see them through that lens. For most folks playing WtA, WtF ended there. It took me 10 years to actually find things i like in WtF for instance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:28:46-07:00","id":1511792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511790#post1511790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just sounds fucking stupid. I assume they dropped that from 2nd for a reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I was interested in that as well. In 2E, the focus is instead on &quot;The Wolf must hunt&quot; and the idea that in order to satisfy their instincts, werewolves just naturally gravitate toward each other. But unless I missed something this idea of Packs having packmembers look for pre-First-Change werewolves and compete with other Packs in recruiting them isn't there anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T09:01:14-07:00","id":1511808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511232-hart-wardens-preview-for-w5?p=1511791#post1511791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it helps, a lot of early Forsaken material was designed in a way to demonstrate how its NOT WtA withouht establishing what it IS. The tonal discussions and disjunctions are very similar in the discussion of the games and thats where the similarity of the games stem from.<br /> <br /> WtF (with a ton of supplements) or WtF2 are games that built their own identity on their own merits.